var MechLoreData = {"20470103": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "Laniakea"}], "introduction": "LTX-210 Aglow\nThis model is a cutting-edge medium maintainer ST developed by Laniakea, part of the innovative R&D line that includes the Arcus and Aurora.\nDesignated as Model III, the Aglow features the advanced L1102-M propulsion system, similar to the Aurora, but with a more aggressive Activity Cycle program tailored for its Manipulator and internal drive. While the Aurora excels in pre-battle protection, the Aglow is designed for relentless combat, prioritizing rapid repairs for STs in danger and stability in high-intensity battles. Unfortunately, the lack of a suitable scenario raises significant concerns for Laniakea and the UNCS Industry and Technology Department about the future of its production line.", "stories": [{"title": "Stolen", "text": "The best time for recovery has passed, and we cannot accept the losses before us—Lab IX's experimental depot has been destroyed. Of our five finished STs, two have been destroyed and one has been stolen... We still don't know how many were involved or who they are... The NDF, tasked with safeguarding the experimental park, has yet to take decisive action. Their response to our requests has been disheartening, offering only the advisement to \"protect yourselves and await the arrival of a rescue team, as we await further directives from our superiors.\" The potential consequences of our competitors or adversaries acquiring the LTX-210 prototype are deeply concerning. The way forward in uncertain.\n— Laniakea Lab IX Researcher", "comment": {"by": "Naomi", "text": "Laniakea's Labs VIII and IX, located in the western part of the mainland, were struck in a sudden, calculated heist in XC 114. The as-yet-undisclosed LTX-210—later known as Aglow—was stolen in the incident. What is suspicious is that this incident came so suddenly. There were no warnings, no shootouts, just a surgical breach in which the perpetrators bypassed the guards and decoy factories to get to Lab IX, responsible for developing Aglow, and left unhindered after acquiring the target. One can't help but wonder... was there inside help?"}}, {"title": "Cut Off", "text": "It's been three months, and we're still at a standstill. Despite promising leads early on, each potential breakthrough abruptly fizzles out, leaving us frustrated and stuck. There are rumors that the GSA has gotten involved, but it's hard to believe they can't catch the thief. This makes me think there's a mole in our midst, someone from within the UNCS military working against us. But why would they do this to us? Laniakea is a trusted military supplier, yet we face constant interference and theft. We've dedicated much of our resources to the UNCS military's ST development, yet they expect us to bear the financial burden. The success of the LTX-210 model is crucial for Laniakea's entry into the free military market, but it seems like the UNCS military keeps moving the goalposts.", "comment": {"by": "Naomi", "text": "The finest intelligence agency in the world? The finest intelligence agency in the world?! The finest intelligence agency in the world?!?!"}}, {"title": "In Vain", "text": "There have been some developments... The military has issued an order to prohibit the commercialization of the LTX-201P. It seems this ST, designed initially as an exclusive model, cannot escape its fate. It seems obvious now who the unexpected mastermind behind this is... Laniakea can only exist as a vassal of the UNCS, explore and develop in the direction intended by the military, and accept funding and orders from within the military... If we can't catch up to Obsidian, it's all for naught... So many people, years, and departments have put so much effort into Laniakea... And now it seems like it was all for nothing."}, {"title": "Change", "text": "It's strange... Lab IX has been shut down for almost two and a half years now, and development of the LTX-210 has long been discontinued. However, we received news of the restructuring of the LTX-210 development line. In addition, upper management also revealed to us that there have been at least 30 orders for the LTX-210 placed with us... This is very suspicious, as the LTX-210, a high-endurance repair ST explicitly designed for high-intensity warfare, should have a minimal range of applications these days...\nLaniakea, the UNCS, and even the whole world are facing changes... Now, the only thing we can hope for is that these changes will be for the better.", "comment": {"by": "Naomi", "text": "Lab IX was restructured around the middle of XC 116, just after the explosion in White Maple... Blair's plan to start a war on the island is well known to all. Let's hope that this disaster set to sweep the world won't come too fiercely and too quickly."}}]}, "30280103": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "Horizon"}], "introduction": "HR-675 Alicorn\nDeveloped by Horizon, this Heavy ST is currently deployed in only a few units of the Dawnstar League Armored Forces.\nFollowing the success of Rex, Horizon introduced this new model. While both Alicorn and Rex are designed for long-range combat, they employ completely opposite design philosophies. If Rex is a glass cannon that sacrifices defense for speed, then Alicorn is a mobile fortress that balances firepower and protection, featuring a complete defensive system. Its composite armor is connected to the fire control system, continuously collecting environmental intel for real-time algorithms, ensuring protection while supporting the pilot's ranged attacks, perfectly showcasing Horizon's expertise in sniper models.", "stories": [{"title": "Unified Offense and Defense", "text": "As early as the Border War, the ST designated HR-675 had already appeared on the battlefield. For strategic reasons, the Dawnstar League Defense Forces sought a mainline unit that combined robust protection with performance superiority—one capable of breaking battlefield deadlock. HR-675 was conceived as an experimental platform under this mandate. Researchers at Horizon outfitted it with heavy structural armor and an advanced fire-control system. This innovative configuration allowed the unit to balance defense and offense simultaneously, enabling it to adapt to highly variable combat environments."}, {"title": "Sleeping Beast", "text": "After being deployed in actual combat, the HR-675 indeed demonstrated excellent performance, even achieving overwhelming victories on some battlefields. However, it also exposed a significant shortcoming that could not be ignored. Due to technical limitations, the regular power system could not support the composite armor and fire control system mounted on the prototype. Technicians adopted a rather aggressive design approach, requiring the main engine of the ST to be synchronized with a large number of special parts for stable operation. This resulted in the maintenance costs of the HR-675 remaining high, even necessitating a dedicated logistics team for handling. Such high maintenance costs drastically reduced its value as a main force ST. Ultimately, the HR-675 lost in the bid to the low-cost, ample production capacity Zealred, and the related production lines were subsequently shelved."}, {"title": "A Legend Rebooted", "text": "When the name HR-675 reappeared in the public eye, it was more than a decade after the war had ended. By then, Rex had achieved great success in the ST market, and Horizon had transformed from an obscure ST manufacturer into a leading company, securing research funds and production cycles several times more generous than before. Although Horizon had a well-established advantage in sniper units, shortly after Rex debuted, excellent sniper models like Blue Bird and Dreadtalon were launched one after another, continuously challenging Horizon's original market dominance. Horizon urgently needed a new product to consolidate its leading position in sniper models—creating an equally outstanding ST that was sufficiently different from Rex became Horizon's top priority. It was at this time that Clark, the then-chief researcher, defied opposition and announced the launch of the experimental unit HR-675, which had been active during the border wars, officially naming it \"Alicorn.\"", "comment": {"by": "Naomi", "text": "Rehashing old ideas is not uncommon in the ST market, however, rehashing something from 20 years ago is."}}, {"title": "Reawakening", "text": "In just a few decades, ST production has already undergone rapid technological changes. Transitioning from HR-675 to the \"Alicorn\" is far from a simple refurbishment for Horizon. From the underlying mainframe to the external fire control system, technicians have drawn on the experience gained from developing Rex, almost completely reconstructing the Alicorn from head to toe. Although the Alicorn still has the drawbacks of high maintenance costs and long production cycles, its outstanding performance on the test field has already won the favor of the Dawnstar League Armored Forces. Meanwhile, due to shifts in market conditions and strategic needs, the shortcomings of the Alicorn are no longer as unacceptable in the new environment as they once were. HR-675 quickly received orders from the DL military after testing and was approved for external market approval.\nUnder similar conditions, completely different results were achieved. Facing this dramatic difference, mainstream external opinion attributes this reversal to postwar doctrinal change—rather than sustaining vast standing forces, the authorities now favor elite, rapidly deployable units capable of decisive superiority in localized theaters—and Alicorn fits this doctrine precisely.", "comment": {"by": "Paloma", "text": "Honestly, when you strip it down, isn't this just an \"HD remaster\" of a discarded oversized toy? Sa— When you grow up, don't become the sort of person who wastes research funds like this, all right?"}}]}, "20520103": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "Laniakea"}], "introduction": "LTX-219 Arbiter\nA medium tactical ST developed by Laniakea. It is a new ST launched in the Arcus-Aurora development line.\nThe LTX-219 inherits the double advantages of the Arcus series tactical ST and the Aurora series engineering ST. Its core Fireweaver Chip can coordinate the firing strategy and strike method of tactical weapons in real-time according to the battlefield situation. Especially in terms of ammo loading and strike coverage, it has achieved a qualitative improvement compared to previous models. The L1102-X propulsion system, iterated from the Arcus, allows the Arbiter to achieve more stable firing conditions in mobile warfare, minimizing the interference of battlefield movement on strike accuracy.", "stories": [{"title": "Demand Slump", "text": "For a military-industrial giant like Laniakea, which serves the UNCS, maintaining multiple ST production lines regardless of cost—and continuously developing STs suited for large-scale warfare—has long been core business. However, shifts in the competitive landscape and setbacks suffered by UNCS forces have led to a sharp decline in internal orders and subsidies. As a result, Laniakea has been forced to shut down several high-cost military ST production lines and research programs, redirecting resources toward externally marketed ST models. After Aglow debuted as the successor to Aurora, the A-series prototype LTX-212 Arcus found itself in an increasingly awkward position. As a top-tier tactical ST, Arcus faces severe challenges in external commercialization. Its L1102-X locomotion drive and the direct-link system designed exclusively for the Nova-Frame offer virtually no commercial viability outside UNCS internal use. For years, Arcus production relied almost entirely on a small number of internal orders. While the unit itself remains exceptional, internal demand has gradually reached saturation, pushing the once-proud Arcus line toward the brink of closure."}, {"title": "Breakthrough Challenge", "text": "To save the Arcus production line from imminent demise, Laniakea has introduced several commercialization plans. For example, they considered downgrading the Arcus by removing high-security technology modules, including the L1102-X propulsion core, and replacing them with regular components for sale. Alternatively, they could leverage existing technological foundations to create a new Tactical ST with commercial potential, entering the lower-tier ST market with differentiation as a selling point. Another option is to sell parts of the Tactical ST support service system, backed by their status as an NDF equipment supplier, to fund other advanced production lines. However, while Laniakea remains undecided, the ST market—especially the Tactical ST market—has undergone drastic changes. The market has seen the emergence of unconventional Tactical STs like the Igniter, which focuses on cost-effectiveness and solo combat, as well as the high-end Mithril from Hermes manufacturer An-Holt. Time is running out for Laniakea, and the market space is shrinking. No matter how you look at it, the once-glorious A-series production line seems destined to meet its end in this internal upheaval."}, {"title": "LTX-219", "text": "The turning point ultimately came from within the UNCS. However, this time it was not from the NDF, but from the UNCS General Security Administration. According to the Administration's requirements, Laniakea undertook the development plan for a new tactical ST, codenamed LTX-219. This tactical ST will not only inherit the technological essence of the Arcus but also incorporate some technologies from its sister models, the Aurora and Aglow, which are repair models. The new tactical ST, developed based on these technological legacies, will not only serve as a lethal weapon for enemy strikes but will also be equipped with enhanced warheads specially developed by Laniakea. These will be used to provide various forms of enhancements to allied STs on the battlefield through firepower projection.", "comment": {"by": "Naomi", "text": "It is important to note that Laniakea's decline in the commercial ST sector is not a matter of quality. On the contrary, tactical STs like Arcus were simply too far ahead of the market, making external commercialization inherently difficult."}}, {"title": "War Factory", "text": "According to information revealed by some insiders within the NDF, Laniakea has already delivered the design plans and prototype of the LTX-219. Although the target pilot remains unknown, recent actions by the GSA suggest that the LTX-219 is intended to adapt to the frontline combat of a certain member of the agency. Meanwhile, Laniakea has also begun to advance the development plan for \"Wide-Area Strike Tactical STs\" represented by the LTX-219. Laniakea's commercialization strategy has been temporarily halted, and it remains the most relied-upon weapons supplier for the NDF, fully absorbing orders from within the UNCS. Undoubtedly, this information has further complicated the increasingly tense border situation. And the official debut of the LTX-219 on the battlefield is likely not far off."}]}, "20270103": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "Laniakea"}], "introduction": "LTX-212 Arcus\nA medium tactical ST developed by Laniakea and planned for deployment in the NDF Forerunner Tactical Strike Squad.\nIt's shoulder is embedded with a synchronize hub, which uses nano-transistor wires to coordinate its Arashium alloy frame's energy distribution with long-range firepower, maximizing efficiency with tactical weapons. In addition, the L1102-X propulsion system installed in the Arcus exhibits similar performance to the L1102-M used in the Aurora, with an optimized OS that significantly improves battlefield reaction speed, allowing for rapid deployment in high-intensity combat.", "stories": [{"title": "Battle-Damaged", "text": "First glimpse of Arcus—Darian's dragged from a net café by UNCS troops. Battle-scarred beauty parks up—dark paint, light stripes, two rockets left. Darian's loving the cockpit view through a massive hole. \"Killer design! Best visibility ever!\"\nCommander: \"Idiot. That's from a pile driver.\"\n\"Oh... you'll fix that, right?\"\nNo answer. Train rolls frontward."}, {"title": "On the Eve of Battle", "text": "Darian thought his mad skills in \"God of the ST\" scored him a spot in the NDF Wrong!\nThe NDF snatched up brainiacs like Darian—multi-lingual data wizards who could pilot cutting-edge steel troopers in a heartbeat. These fresh recruits plugged the gaps left by fallen comrades.\n\"Mastering an Arcus? That's gotta take years!\" Darian mused.\nThe commander's voice crackled: \"Moron! You've already nailed rocket launches. Get to your mark, await orders, lock on, and pull the trigger. Simple!\"\n\"Right... Just like the last guy who bit the dust in this very seat?\"\nBefore he could get a response, Dawnstar shells rained down, screaming at Darian to move his metal ass."}, {"title": "The Incident", "text": "Post-victory, Arcus gets its fix. Full armor, precision strikes, dual-shoulder rockets - pure fear factor. Darian's grown into it, both restored to glory. But one ST can't save UNCS. After Belsuth falls, troops pull back. Time's running out.\n\"Mission over, Commander? Just mastered this beast!\"\n\"Idiot. Back to your café. Keep the skills, leave the ST.\"\n\"UNCS might need me... someday?\"\nSilence. Just a phone number on his comm."}, {"title": "Written in the Stars", "text": "Found Darian in a Tiktaalik wreck. NDF needed bodies on the line. Elite pilot, elite duty. His last message unanswered."}]}, "20190103": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "Laniakea"}], "introduction": "LTX-201P Aurora\nA medium maintainer ST developed by Laniakea. Its performance is on par with the DL's Blazer and it enjoys a respectable reputation among the UNCS Border Forces.\nIt is equipped with the L1102-M propulsion system and has been specialized to carry a manipulator on its back, allowing it to maintain its balance while executing repair commands. The additional scanner can detect manipulator damage, enabling more precise repairs.\nCurrently, it is only deployed by the NDF, and there are no plans for commercialization.", "stories": [{"title": "Aurora Rises", "text": "The Milkhama War proved the value of heavy firepower and STs. Post-war focus shifted to enhancing individual ST combat power, making logistics support crucial. The ST Aurora began as a logistics unit, designed for long-range support, ammo transport, and infantry protection. Its original ammo rack design remains lost to time.", "comment": {"by": "Grant", "text": "Logistics STs get the job done. Repair STs do it better."}}, {"title": "The Transformation of the Viceroy", "text": "The ST Aurora's shift from logistics to repair came after the new viceroy's appointment. Despite his Milkhama War experience, the viceroy's stance on firepower-logistics doctrine remained unclear, though he favored massive war machines."}, {"title": "The Viceroy's Decision", "text": "The repair unit transition faced resistance. Long development times, high costs, and hard-to-measure results made research institutes hesitant. Field pilots' requests for repair units were overshadowed by demands for combat power. Though many question the viceroy's frontline understanding, Aurora's performance now shows promise after years of investment.", "comment": {"by": "Grant", "text": "Preached to a hundred about us machinists being frontline heroes. Ninety-nine couldn't care less. The last guy? \"Cool story bro, now about that hotshot ace who solo'd the outpost...\""}}, {"title": "No Waves", "text": "Aurora hit the Foren border running. Every squad wanted one, no complaints, unheard of. Viceroy went broke backing it. Black market gold now, but no plans to commercialize.", "comment": {"by": "Naomi", "text": "No ordinary politician—makes enemies everywhere and hoards power. A typical suit would never dare."}}]}, "20430103": {"profile": [], "introduction": "MCT-AP07 霸王\n全称为「塔罗斯精神力机甲亚太七号机·霸王」，隶属于亚太战区，适配驾驶员为郑乐萱。\n该机收集了原属世界秦末时期著名将领、军事家西楚霸王项羽的精神粒子作为动力炉内核，以高强度框架与诸多可拓展模块构筑机身，并搭载了独特的玄门磁极引擎·景——这一系列设计确保霸王拥有极为出色的防御与火力投射能力，足以在任何战场胜任「前沿支点」的职责。"}, "10510103": {"profile": [], "introduction": "DD-217 奔霄\n由神州设计师主导设计，多尔工业与角雕商会联合开发的轻型机兵。\n奔霄在多尔工业成熟的第三世代机兵通用框架上，引入了大量神州独有的机械设计，这使得该型机兵在外型上独树一帜。精细调整的超高增压发动机与XF4S轻量框架为其取得了防护与机动近乎完美的平衡，安装于腿部的KERBS动能循环增强系统与足部驱动轮又为其提供了优秀的战时机动和瞬时输出功率。此外，由角雕商会自行开发的试验型辅助模组「逐鸿核心」配置于机师舱内部，可自动完成对动能的精准化回收与增强，大幅提升作战效能。\n对米赫玛岛而言，无论是在技术层面还是政治层面上，这无疑都是一型有着特殊意义的机兵。"}, "20130103": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "Kamadar"}], "introduction": "KX-066 Blazer\nThe \"Mobile Repair Station.\" A medium maintainer ST produced by Kamadar Corporation, featuring a unique assist system.\nThe prototype for this ST was the Kamadar engineering SL - KX-037, later improved by the machinist Champmathieu Favre and utilized by rebels. After the Dawnstar League confiscated this model, it was handed over to Kamadar for reverse engineering and optimization, further improving its armor level and terrain adaptability. It was then renamed, put into production, and put into use by the DLAF.", "stories": [{"title": "Embargo Regulations", "text": "Dawnstar League regulations forced Kamadar to impose a military ST embargo on Siniestro ports. The ban limits ST models, weapon systems, armor, engine output, and fire control chips to prevent civilian STs from militarization. Ironically, the next year saw a surge in specialized rebel STs that skirted these restrictions.", "comment": {"by": "Seven", "text": "STs, like life, adapt and survive."}}, {"title": "Best Arrangement", "text": "The Blazer's prototype KX-037: a mid-size mecha disguised as a logging and repair unit. This mechanical marvel excels at maintenance, its frame packed with modular spaces. When shipped, it's a hollow shell. But in the right hands, those voids transform. High-grade armor plating materializes, and weapon ports emerge as if by magic. It's the perfect Trojan horse—innocent on the outside, a war machine within.", "comment": {"by": "Seven", "text": "My mod skills? Just keeping Milkhama's tradition alive."}}, {"title": "Irregular Transformation", "text": "The Siniestro rebels rock a sick battle strat. They snag a KX-037, soup it up with a beast engine and armor thick as hell, morphing it into a rolling repair rig.\nTheir combat formation's all about that KX-037. NDF hits other rebel STs? The KX-037's there, patching 'em up non-stop. NDF tries to take down the KX-037? Rebel STs get two shots at wrecking NDF units before that armored beast falls.\nThe mastermind behind this mod, Champmathieu Favre, got busted in 112. Slapped with 50 years hard time. Word on the street? The outlaw bolted that same year. Still in the wind, evading justice.", "comment": {"by": "Seven", "text": "50 years from uncle? Too long."}}, {"title": "Serve Me", "text": "The Dawnstar League snagged a bunch of souped-up KX-037s from the Siniestro rebels during a series of raids. These Frankenstein mechs were shipped to Kamadar's lab for a full teardown.\nThe eggheads cracked the rebels' upgrade code after an intense study sesh. Kamadar took these street-smart mods, cranked them to eleven, and beefed up the armor and off-road capabilities. Reborn as the \"KX-066 Blazer,\" this beast quickly became the DLAF's go-to maintainer ST, setting a new bar for performance.", "comment": {"by": "Seven", "text": "Outrage at stolen tech! Where's justice?"}}]}, "20220103": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "Obsidian"}], "introduction": "OS-79 Blue Bird\nA cutting-edge medium ST developed by Obsidian that has gained attention for its outstanding performance and unique appearance.\nEquipped with the BM battlefield analysis module, built using data from the legendary XR. By receiving real-time information from reconnaissance devices, the Blue Bird's unique OS quickly generates detailed posture analysis to analyze the behavioral patterns of enemy STs, allowing pilots to make tactical adjustments and launch powerful attacks on weak points in the enemy line.", "stories": [{"title": "Afternoon Conspiracy", "text": "Alright, here's the deal. I know you'll ruin my sunny vacation if I don't talk. Five minutes? Please. We Obsidian folks aren't lab rats. Let's hit that corner café. Their cappuccino's killer. I'll tell you about Blue Bird."}, {"title": "Blue Bird Aesthetics", "text": "\"Top-grade strength, adaptive combat system, got it? Want more? That's the tech specs... Oh, you mean the look? Revolutionary. Pure war-aesthetic perfection. If it looks lethal, fights lethal.\""}, {"title": "Friendly Banter", "text": "Affirmative! It's the top-tier medium ST in the mecha arena!\nHold up, you mean that enigmatic prototype? No contest there. XR's a ghost—lone unit, phantom pilot, MIA status. No combat stats, no safety specs. Blue Bird's your rock-solid ride compared to that vapor-mech.\n*Slurp* Ah, last drop of lukewarm java. How's that info dump sitting with you?\nDigging it, huh? Craving the intel? Ha! Pocket that Milkhama Dollar. This Obsidian researcher's legit, on payroll. No need for press cash here.", "comment": {"by": "Naomi", "text": "Good researchers handle media heat too."}}, {"title": "Marshall and the Doctor", "text": "Doc: \"Marshall, you leaked Blue Bird?\"\nMarshall: \"Guilty.\"\nDoc: \"Orders flooding in... still unsure of its battlefield role.\"\nMarshall: \"Doc, you know it's cutting-edge. Just bad at selling it.\"\nDoc: \"How'd you pitch it?\"\nMarshall: \"Groundbreaking design, battlefield beauty... Let me get you fresh coffee.\"", "comment": {"by": "Naomi", "text": "A ST researcher who can't sell ain't worth their coffee beans."}}]}, "30270103": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "Kamadar"}], "introduction": "KX-101HA Colossus\nManufactured by Kamadar, this heavy ST is the culmination of second-generation technology.\nAlthough a newly released model, the KX-101HA Colossus does not rely on a new design as its selling point. Instead, it integrates a large amount of mature and reliable existing technology—heavy composite armor, high-capacity weapon hardpoints, a streamlined shield generator, localized tactical data links, and more. These battle-tested technologies work smoothly together under the integration of the Iron Rain Transmuter, pushing the Colossus's basic performance to the extreme—even significantly ahead of some third-generation STs in certain parameters.", "stories": [{"title": "Featured Unit", "text": "After the Milkhama War, major defense groups pushed forward with advanced mech development, but Kamadar appeared slow to react, only launching its next-gen program in XC 113. Combined with earlier missteps on the Heracles project, many believed Kamadar would fall behind in this quiet arms race.\nFive years later, Kamadar released the KX-098 Odysseus. Its strong performance quickly won over the market and drew attention to Kamadar's future lineup. According to insider reports, the company plans to unveil a surprising new unit in December, XC 118, sparking widespread discussion among military enthusiasts."}, {"title": "Unexpected Design", "text": "In December, XC 118, Kamadar officially held its product launch. Most expected another high-end unit like Odysseus, but what they revealed instead was something completely unexpected—an \"King of the Old Era,\" the KX-101HA Colossus.\nThe unit featured heavy Composite Armor, extensive weapon mounts, and integrated proven systems such as a basic shield generator and battlefield data sync modules. Despite relying on mature technology, it achieved strong overall balance. In raw performance, Colossus was a powerhouse, even surpassing some third-generation units in certain metrics. However, while its performance was recognized by military personnel and enthusiasts, it failed to align with the market's demand for cutting-edge designs. Combined with its relatively high cost, its reception remained lukewarm."}, {"title": "Mobile Fortress", "text": "While the market response was lukewarm, the UNCS quickly recognized the Colossus's practical value as a war machine. Its heavy armor allowed it to hold the line in direct engagements, while its large payload capacity meant it could deploy shield systems and still operate heavy weapons like Rail Guns. After securing military orders, Kamadar leveraged its strong production capacity and delivered the first batch of mass-produced units in just over two weeks. In small-scale, dispersed conflicts against insurgents and hostile mercenaries, the Colossus performed beyond expectations. Despite limited mobility, it proved highly effective as a mobile fortress, providing command support and sustained firepower on the battlefield."}, {"title": "Administration Strategy", "text": "As the UNCS began deploying the Colossus, the GSA's armaments division also took notice. While its design didn't fit traditional special operations, the worsening situation on Milkhama and Governor Rosemary Jean's hardline stance on military affairs made a frontline powerhouse like the Colossus a necessary asset. After procuring two batches from Kamadar, the GSA assigned some units to elite agents for direct combat, while distributing others to aligned non-state forces, including incorporated mercenary groups, cooperative crime families, and former resistance factions. These deployments significantly boosted their ability to stand against regular forces. Rumors even suggest that a single Colossus played a decisive role in the mech battle at Kadrey."}]}, "20600103": {"profile": [], "introduction": "HRX-112VE 弥造者\n以海莉丝的设计为基础，经地平线公司、防卫军先进武器研究院先后开发，由维斯珀尔最终完成的中型机兵，也是世界上第一部真正的第四世代机兵。\n该机装备了两组新式岚物质自循环引擎，且与全身钢岚合金框架直接链接，不仅可以提供强大的出力，还可通过施加精确的电磁影响，即时控制各处的岚粒子压缩与释放，使得该机在维持较轻重量的同时拥有远超常规的机械强度。此外，全新设计的通用武装接口使得该机不仅可以兼容多型常规武装，还可在特定条件下将岚粒子高效应用于战斗之中。这一系列先进但又过于复杂的机体设计带来了极大的不稳定性，曾一度被认为无法投入实用，但在海莉丝借助「遗产」之力完成了「真知系统」与「帕姆斯阵列」统筹其系统运作之后，HRX-112VE弥造者真正成为了维斯珀尔撼动局势的最终兵器。"}, "30110103": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "UKB-1"}], "introduction": "HU-35 Dias\nA heavy ST produced by the UKB-1, and ordered and equipped by the NDF.\nThe Dias is equipped with the \"Bloodlust\" core and was initially smuggled into the UNCS for use in underground mech fights. The UNCS military has since seized these black market STs and integrated them into its fighting force.", "stories": [{"title": "Made in Ovett", "text": "Dias appears in UNCS Viceroy Guard and Ashes arsenal. UKB-1 production reaches unexpected UNCS deployment."}, {"title": "Competitive Type", "text": "Prepare for mecha mayhem! The Milkhama underground fight scene was once ruled by a beast of a Steel Trooper called \"Fury.\" This heavy-hitting monster wasn't your run-of-the-mill mass-produced unit. No way! The Ovett Principality's UKB-1 Factory 11 custom-built this bad boy for the underground ring, aiming to dominate ST sports and cash in on the global craze. Why? Factory Seven blew their budget on the Gillesrais project, forcing UKB-1 to get creative with their cash flow.\nWhile other STs duke it out on the battlefield, Fury's built for one thing: total ring domination. This mechanical marvel can bust out the legendary Ovett Extra Stance and unleash a devastating long-range straight punch that'll make your circuits sizzle. From its killer joint design to its razor-sharp optics, every inch of Fury is engineered for one purpose, to lay the smackdown in the boxing ring!", "comment": {"by": "Hong", "text": "Dias still gives me chills. Hit him a hundred times, miss once, you're toast."}}, {"title": "Wrath of a Common Man", "text": "The viceroy's arrival brought hope to Milkhama. As factories reopened, underground ST fighters remained restless. At White Maple, a ST Fury burst from shipping containers, decimating half the viceroy's guard. The assassination failed—the viceroy, an ace pilot himself, survived. Surprisingly, he pardoned the assassin, recruiting them. The ST Fury now stands guard behind Blair, transformed from rebel to divine protector.", "comment": {"by": "Naomi", "text": "Reports confirm it: Viceroy's got Dias under some kind of dark control."}}, {"title": "Recommission", "text": "After rigorous testing, Fury's impressive military potential catches the NDF's attention, leading them to commission its combat variant from UKB-1. Factory 11 begins producing the military version, designated Dias. Despite significant orders, mass production hits a snag—the ST's competition-grade design demands elite pilots. Only a select few Dias units meet quality standards, joining the NDF's ranks as specialized STs in the viceroy's guard detail."}]}, "10110103": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "Obsidian"}], "introduction": "OS-07X Dopplesoldner\nOne of Obsidian's high-performance light STs, developed based on the OS-06F Diana's combat data.\nAs a highly maneuverable execution model, it is equipped with the \"Zweihander\" combat core, a modification of the \"Eden Core.\"\nThe balance between the limbs and torso on this ST has been carefully calibrated to maximize it's killing power.", "stories": [{"title": "Unknown Power", "text": "The Dopplesoldner, Obsidian's classified experimental ST, specializes in decapitation strikes, rivaling Doll Industry's Glasya. Several test units were supplied to the UNCS under research pretenses through secret NDF agreements. As one of Obsidian's three premier L-Type STs, seven-plus units serve with the Predators squad under a female pilot's command. While their covert missions draw public criticism and ethical debates, the Dopplesoldner's record speaks volumes—over 100 next-gen STs destroyed. Its presence typically spells doom for opponents, with just one loss against the Ashes in two years of deployment.", "comment": {"by": "Marcus", "text": "The Ashes had Principality troops in their ranks back then."}}, {"title": "Shadow Warhorse", "text": "Obsidian's zero-tolerance for failure drives radical changes to the Dopplesoldner and its pilots. The new model trades armor for devastating offensive power, featuring an advanced neural interface that only elite Predator pilots can handle. These mysterious operators grow more enigmatic with each deployment of the enhanced ST."}, {"title": "Hidden in the Mist", "text": "Official records show only two documented Predator squad engagements, suggesting either increased covert operations or deeper mission secrecy. In their lone confirmed clash with the Ashes, the Dopplesoldner-equipped team fought to a stalemate. No further encounters between these forces are on record.", "comment": {"by": "Marcus", "text": "The old guard's gone, wiped out in the clash. But Yevgeny's Titan acquisition? That's our game-changer. Without it, we'd be just another ragtag militia in Milkhama's warzone."}}, {"title": "Balance of Power", "text": "Recent Obsidian upgrades to the Dopplesoldner aim to maintain its edge over rival STs. Despite fierce competition with Glasya, pilot skill remains the decisive factor, not targeting systems, frame design, or weapon loadouts.", "comment": {"by": "Marcus", "text": "Light STs need ace pilots more than upgrades."}}]}, "30150103": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "Doll Industries"}], "introduction": "DD-360 Dragonrider\nA heavy ST manufactured by Dole Industries.\nThe shoulders feature an aberrant Steelstorm frame design with an expanded variable-liquid core. It can maximize shoulder kinetic output according to the pilot's combat habits, enabling more powerful and agile melee strikes.", "stories": [{"title": "New Design", "text": "Dragonrider is a heavy ST developed by Doll Industries to consolidate its leading position in close-combat models. According to the information released by the company at an official press conference, the external armor of this model draws on advanced designs inspired by the traditional elements of a mysterious Eastern country and has undergone a comprehensive upgrade in terms of protection and kinetic energy systems, fully integrating them with its attack methods. The shoulders are equipped with an expanded built-in variable liquid core called \"Enlightenment,\" which can maximize shoulder kinetic energy based on the pilot's operating habits, allowing for more vital, more flexible combat strikes."}, {"title": "R&D Blockage", "text": "An external business analyst has claimed that Glasya's commercial success greatly inspired Doll Industries' ST R&D department. After absorbing a large amount of feedback from frontline pilots and research experience from other technical departments, Doll Industries decided to reform its existing heavy ST R&D line and invested more funds and manpower specifically for the development of close-combat models. This decision led to several heavy experimental models, including the DD-360. However, a revolutionary and influential combat ST capable of achieving their expected goals and thrusting them into the ST market has yet to appear.", "comment": {"by": "Grant", "text": "The folks from the Doll family have indeed achieved impressive results in their close-combat model. In addition to the complete ST, their replacement parts are popular items on the market."}}, {"title": "Astonishing Rebirth", "text": "As the release date nears, the business and R&D departments at Doll Industries are still determining the upcoming experimental machine. An email from a respected Doll Family member changed the fate of the DD-360, breathing new life into the struggling R&D line with a revolutionary design concept. This revitalized the project overnight, leading to the grand unveiling of the heavy-duty combat machine, \"Dragonrider,\" leaving intelligence agents and brokers in the dark about the email's contents that transformed the fate of the DD-360.", "comment": {"by": "Naomi", "text": "The digital footprint of this young woman is so elusive—it makes me ponder whether she's effectively concealing her tracks or my access to Skynet needs to be elevated. Further investigation is warranted."}}, {"title": "A Mysterious Letter", "text": "\"...The beauty and innovation I've encountered here have genuinely expanded my world. Please understand my wish to extend my stay—the promise of discovery calls to me. I plan to return home next month...\nOur project's challenges reached my ear, and serendipitously, an old friend introduced me to potential solutions here. You'll find their details attached...\nAlso, I've picked out some local delicacies to share with everyone upon my return.\nWishing you and Father good health.\"\n- Excerpt from Alyson Doll's Letter Home"}]}, "10180103": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "Obsidian"}], "introduction": "OS-09S Dreadtalon\nOne of Obsidian's high-performance light STs, developed based on the OS-06F Diana's combat data.\nThis ST is designed for precision strikes and excels at processing battlefield information, boasting a high efficiency rate in actual combat.\nEquipped with the \"Dominator\" combat core, this unit can assist the pilot in completing a range of actions such as surveillance, positioning, aiming, and striking.", "stories": [{"title": "Information Warfare", "text": "Obsidian's Dreadtalon: A mech masterpiece of modern warfare. Powered by Diana's cutting-edge tech, this beast is built for one thing: lethal precision. The Dominator Locator is its beating heart, fusing real-time data and tactical planning to unleash devastating strikes. When Dreadtalon joins the Kill Streak, enemies don't stand a chance. This isn't just a mech; it's the future of combat, ready to dominate the battlefield in a heartbeat."}, {"title": "Tactical Core", "text": "The \"Dominator Locator\" core's lightning-fast battlefield analysis pinpoints targets and streamlines attacks from recon to launch. This cutting-edge tech propels Dreadtalon to elite status alongside Dopplesoldner and Twilight Fang as Obsidian's top light STs. Its unmatched tactical edge and stellar combat record have made Dreadtalon a hot commodity in the mech market."}, {"title": "Beech", "text": "Dreadtalon's combat data from UNCS ops confirms its killer strike efficiency. In \"Operation Beech,\" multi-terminal Order Strike mode orchestrated a symphony of destruction. Light, medium, and heavy STs, backed by Self-Propelled Artillery, unleashed a 360-degree assault. Result: Dawnstar League's stealth squad—5 STs and 3 transports, wiped off the grid.", "comment": {"by": "Marcus", "text": "Heads up! This bad boy packs a punch like a grizzled vet from the last war."}}, {"title": "Hardcore Cooperation", "text": "The Dreadtalon's cutting-edge \"Dominator Locator\" fire control system is just the tip of the iceberg. This mech's hardware is primed for the toughest missions. Memory alloy infused throughout its steel frame ensures lightning-fast target acquisition and startup. While it may not withstand heavy artillery or high-impact strikes, the Dreadtalon's true power lies in its swift strikes. In just 20 seconds, it gathers intel, locks on, and unleashes a devastating coordinated attack with its squad, obliterating targets before they can react.", "comment": {"by": "Marcus", "text": "The ultimate defense? Go on the offensive! Now, where can we score some of those sweet \"Dominator Locator\" cores, my friend?"}}]}, "20180103": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "Obsidian"}], "introduction": "XR-03-E Erinys\nA Medium ST jointly developed by UNCS and Obsidian. Nominally the successor to \"XR-Rebirth\" and \"XR-Judgment,\" its customization philosophy remains singular in purpose: to serve the transformed Rosa Diaz alone. In addition to matrixing the \"Mirror Core\" mounted on the XR, it also enhances the linkage between assault and tactical weaponry according to Rosa Diaz's personal combat style. Due to anomalous fluctuations observed in XR-03-E's arashi material structure while piloted by Rosa, relevant researchers have already initiated a follow-up investigation. What cannot be denied is this: XR-03-E's rebirth has only one objective—to once again become the blade with which Rosa Diaz passes judgment upon all.", "stories": [{"title": "Eyewitness Report", "text": "\"XR-03-E, a Generation X model secretly constructed after the White Maple unrest in May, XC 116. Although this ST is nominally an enhancement of the XR exclusively for Rosa Diaz, the XR was nearly completely scrapped upon recovery, making the XR-03-E a completely reconstructed new unit. This model and its mysterious pilot were sighted in Thepia, East Milkhama in June, XC 118, followed by multiple active records in the East Desert, Port Kelvin, and within West Milkhama. It fell into silence after the Blair Rebellion at the end of XC 118. According to the limited intel available, this model has inherited the XR's formidable performance and visible support for biomechanical integration. Although it is currently impossible to determine whether the powerful combat characteristics displayed in video archives primarily originate from the ST or the pilot, it is certain that the ST performance of the XR-03-E has already far surpassed all standard generation STs.\""}, {"title": "Application Rejected", "text": "\"Ada Diaz rejected the 'Valkyrie Seizure Plan' proposed by Defense Camp staff, instead exercising her privilege as a Super Pilot to independently infiltrate West Milkhama via an alternative route... and during this operation, she did not pilot ▇▇▇▇▇▇. Although Ada Diaz ultimately succeeded in retrieving the NDF's Valkyrie, the XR-03-E was unexpectedly recovered by Obsidian. Intel regarding Rosa Diaz and the XR-03-E may have already been leaked, suggesting a possible secret trade between the Super Pilot and Obsidian... It is foreseeable that Obsidian will inevitably intervene in the research and supervision of Rosa Diaz, as well as the subsequent renovation of the XR-03-E... In response, the Oceanic Conclave has decided to temporarily detain Rosa Diaz on Milkhama Island, under the care of the Reversion Squad to advance related research... Meanwhile, the application from Cicero Wright has been reviewed. The application was rejected for his involvement in the related research...\"", "comment": {"by": "Cicero", "text": "Fools! Don't you know who designed this ST? That fool Winston Gresham! I worked on XR's design—I know that idiot better than anyone. I even contributed to the XR prototype myself... and you didn't bring me in!?"}}, {"title": "Unfulfilled Wish", "text": "\"I know this well. Beyond the battalion encampment lies Milkhama. Beyond Milkhama, the home continent. And beyond that, the world itself... The world is vast beyond measure—yet only this cramped cockpit can truly be called my place of refuge. I have to save my sister. No matter the cost. No matter the sacrifice. Even if I must sink into ruin myself—I will not hesitate. And I must save others as well. The girls who, simply because they resemble me, are forced to shoulder the same curse. The new recruits who suffer merely because I exist. I will win every battle. I will purge every enemy. But for now... only you remain by my side, XR. I'm sorry—truly—for making you bear this weight with me. If the day comes when we fall together, and I still have not fulfilled that vow... then that would be my greatest regret.\""}, {"title": "Confidential Brief", "text": "\"It has now been confirmed that during the test cycle prepared for her by the UNCS, the arashi-matter transmission structure of XR has undergone a fundamental change. This change was not caused by any external intervention, but by the arashi matter itself undergoing transformation—yes, identical to what was observed in Ada Diaz. In other words, the arashi matter responded to her. XR-03-E is becoming stronger, and increasingly aligned with her 'intent.' The ST's operational patterns are no longer simple behavior mappings; they are becoming a part of her. Although the pace of change remains slow, no one knows where this evolution will ultimately lead. From the perspective of corporate interests, we cannot afford to relinquish such a valuable test subject, nor can we allow ourselves to lose our advantage at the forefront of arashi-matter research. XR-03-E will be returned to Rosa Diaz—to become her new cage.\"", "comment": {"by": "Morgana", "text": "First, the bad news: Ada's entourage is keeping a close eye on Rosa, so the original plan is off... But we all know what kind of person Rosa is, don't we? So have patience... and a little more patience still... In the end, we will get what we want."}}]}, "30140103": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "SEED"}], "introduction": "SAT-331 Euclase\nAs SEED's first premium model, this heavy ST showcases exceptional craftsmanship.\nWith versatile angled armor and armament detection modules on both shoulders, it offers affordability and remarkable versatility. Despite the potential for battlefield damage to its external gear, the Euclase delivers outstanding effectiveness, embodying SEED's commitment to value for money.", "stories": [{"title": "Transformation Crisis", "text": "SEED, initially dominant in labor-intensive ST production, faced challenges when the first-generation military STs phased out after the border war ceasefire, and the influx of second-hand STs and new competitors in the Milkhama region reduced SEED's market share. By XC 110, only the Mandrill model remained competitive. Furthermore, the shift to small-scale conflicts eroded SEED's advantage in heavy firepower production. This has made adaptation crucial for SEED's survival."}, {"title": "Gem Series", "text": "SEED's key advantage is its exceptional cost-effectiveness, derived from offshore production facilities.\nTo combat rising labor costs, the company launched an R&D initiative to establish a high-end product line in Milkhama in August of XC 104, named the \"Gem Series,\" which emphasizes unbeatable value while enhancing quality and modern warfare adaptability."}, {"title": "Industry Consensus", "text": "SEED is set to enter the high-end market, generating widespread interest in the ST community. However, doubts linger about its potential success, given significant industry shifts and competition from established players like Obsidian and Laniakea. Financial giants like the Doll Group and the rising stars of the East, Katana, further compound the challenges, leading to widespread anticipation of SEED's struggles with its new product line.", "comment": {"by": "Arthur", "text": "Let them say what they want, SEED is one of the few conscientious manufacturers in the world. I'll always be a loyal SEED fanboy, forever!"}}, {"title": "Rising Star", "text": "In July of XC 109, the launch of Euclase, the first product in the Gem series silenced critics instantly. Its cutting-edge design, flawless performance, and unmistakable SEED manufacturing excellence left the public speechless. The boldness and innovation of the machine's manufacturer were evident, especially with its impressive price-performance ratio. Despite concerns about its latest exposed fire detectors and the absence of specialized armor, the Euclase soared to the top of sales charts, rescuing SEED Manufacturing from a pivotal juncture and rekindling pilot enthusiasm. Perhaps, to critics and technology enthusiasts pursuing high-end perfection, the rationale behind its design might remain a mystery forever.", "comment": {"by": "Grant", "text": "Who uses these STs? The pilots! With the search unit, fire detectors, and high-density armor plates...you name it, they've got it! Concealment and vulnerability issues can be solved by adding spare parts or installing a shield. Those high-end ST manufacturers always try to add gimmicks and raise prices, but Euclase slapped them back to reality this time!"}}]}, "30360103": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "Kamadar"}], "introduction": "ROG-FE01 Eye of Faith\nA Heavy ST jointly developed by renowned hardware manufacturer ROG and Kamadar. The design adopts the cutting-edge and trendy style of the ROG series, equipped with multiple glowing light strips. Internally, it uses Kamadar's mature solutions, with an industry-leading transmission system and arashi alloy frame, allowing the Eye of Faith to stand out in protracted battles.", "stories": [{"title": "Eye of Faith", "text": "With the continuous advancement of arashium ST technology, the arashium ST market is also expanding. More and more cross-industry brands are beginning to pay attention to the dynamics of the ST field. As a leader in hardware brands, ROG showcased their jointly developed arashium ST with Kamadar at the new year's Milthus Mech Exhibition—the ROG S.T. Fearless Eye, Eye of Faith."}, {"title": "Beyond the Peak", "text": "Known as a symbol of cutting-edge hardware culture, ROG selected its ST partner with care. Among multiple proposals, Kamadar—renowned for technical rigor and quality control—aligned closely with ROG's design philosophy, giving rise to the ROG-FE01 platform."}, {"title": "Polymorphic Channels", "text": "Kamadar's expertise lies in Heavy STs, exemplified by its best-selling KX-075 Heracles. Eye of Faith adopts Kamadar's industry-leading heavy ST solution, featuring a fluid generator and Hyper Frame. This configuration enables exceptional endurance in prolonged engagements, providing reliable protection for allied ST units."}, {"title": "Committed to Progress", "text": "Upon debut, Eye of Faith immediately drew attention for its striking visual design: bold color schemes, luminous energy bands, intermittent holographic projections, and a solid, imposing silhouette. It has since won multiple ST design awards, with buyers increasingly evaluating its combat capabilities. As manufacturers deepen collaboration with top designers, more STs balancing aesthetics and battlefield utility are expected to follow."}]}, "20540103": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "Obsidian"}], "introduction": "OS-10S Fenrisúlfr\nA medium melee ST designed by the Cicero Laboratory and workshopped by Obsidian. It is a contemporary of the OS-13S Hela.\nEquipped with the Hrodvitnir Unit, it can bypass most onboard interference systems to lock onto enemy units and provide powerful kinetic energy for the OS-10S's pursuit-strike system. Due to the fall of the Blair regime, the OS-10S was never mass-produced, and the few test types in existence were stored in the Predator Laboratory on Milkhama Island, eventually taken over by the UNCS. Whether Fenrisúlfr will achieve new headway in positioning and tech innovation remains uncertain.", "stories": [{"title": "Lost Archives 01", "text": "\"I thought I had found an employer with true foresight, but it turns out you're just as foolish as those factionalists! My Underworld series are masterpieces that transcend time, flawless in every way! Each machine soldier can become the absolute ruler in its field! Yet you chose the worst one among them, nitpicking the basic data report, and even questioning my expertise? Just wait, I will find buyers who are more generous and visionary than you! You'll be crushed by my masterpieces on the battlefield!\" —Cicero Laboratory Voice Archive", "comment": {"by": "Fenrir", "text": "You claim the design inspiration came from your own hard work? Please. You only got the idea after watching me fight. Still, since you named the ST after me, I'll let it slide this time."}}, {"title": "Lost Archives 02", "text": "\"...The situation is becoming increasingly severe, and we are running out of time! The items in Laboratory AC-7 must be relocated! Items assessed as non-transferable should be destroyed on-site immediately. If these items fall into the hands of the GSA, the consequences will be unimaginable... Catherine of the Predators has already set out for the Laboratory, and the NDF in the Mouty Mountains region will assist us in completing the transfer operation. However, forces from Free Milkhama and the GKD Parcel Service are also advancing toward the target location. Members remaining inside the laboratory should prepare for defense, do their best to delay the enemy's main force, and wait for reinforcements to arrive!\" —Laboratory AC-7 Voice Archive", "comment": {"by": "Movme", "text": "Seriously, Fenrir? You don't even have a Medium ST pilot license, and you're claiming you designed this thing? If you weren't riding my reputation, no one would know who you are."}}, {"title": "Lost Archives 03", "text": "\"I saw the ST. The new close-combat unit built on the same technology as OS-13S. Scarring on its exterior indicates the Predators attempted to relocate it. When relocation proved impossible, they attempted to destroy OS-10S using conventional weapons. After repeated failures, it was abandoned in the medical waste bay. According to inspection reports, OS-10S's external armor strength far exceeded Predator estimates. Its internal arashi-material frame even demonstrated partial self-repair while the ST remained inactive. It is now clear that during the relocation-and-destruction catastrophe, the Predators overlooked their most valuable asset. These next-generation experimental STs will form the cornerstone of our next phase of armament expansion.\" —Sunset Valley Ground Forces Camp Voice Archive", "comment": {"by": "Fenrir", "text": "Huh? Riding your rep? Who in the entire Northwest Jungle hasn't heard of Fenrir of the Electric Eels?! When I chose my name, this ST's materials were still a mile underground. This thing's riding my damn reputation!"}}, {"title": "Lost Archives 04", "text": "\"...I know what you're worried about, Colonel. The military's influence in Milkhama has indeed changed, but that doesn't mean we don't have cards to play against the bureaucrats. During the last moments of Blair's political career, many important secrets were transferred from Milkhama Island. We have followed these secret clues and recovered many valuable assets on the island... Whether it's STs or technology. I believe there are treasures among these assets that will catch your eye... Please trust this, Colonel Wyatt Morgan—whether you accept this gift or not, the military will always stand behind you.\" —Unknown Area Voice Recording", "comment": {"by": "Naomi", "text": "Wait. Why did this archive derail like this? How did those two even find this file? Who keeps self-searching nonstop on Skynet?"}}]}, "30050103": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "Horizon"}], "introduction": "HR-805 FierceJaw\nA Heavy ST manufactured by Horizon.\nFierceJaw is an innovative iteration of its predecessor, the HR-801. The iteration process took into account the self-modifications made by frontline pilots, adding numerous protection plates to the cockpit while significantly optimizing the disassembly of panels and external attachments. This series of iterations allows FierceJaw to better cooperate with Engineering STs in battlefield engagements and adjust its armor according to specific battlefield conditions.", "stories": [{"title": "Free Modification", "text": "During Smith's daily check of the FierceJaw, he found one unit with its hip armor plate removed and the shoulder joint coming loose. The tool marks made it quite clear the pilot had modified it without authorization—something strictly forbidden by DL regulations. The culprit soon showed himself: it was Jack. \"You can't do this,\" Smith said. \"You're going to get both of us in serious trouble.\" \"Right now, our priority is surviving against the UNCS forces,\" Jack replied. \"As for military orders, to hell with them.\"", "comment": {"by": "Naomi", "text": "As far as I know, the earliest batch of FierceJaw didn't have standout performance and were assigned to be second-line combat units. What happened to turn this model into the go-to ST for elite DLAF pilots...?"}}, {"title": "Performance Surge", "text": "After weighing it up, Smith decided the missing armor could pass a wear-and-tear, the sort of thing that might drop off an older unit. He chose not to file a report—a machinist, he felt, needed some leeway. But soon he spotted something much harder to overlook. The half-track drive system built into the legs of this FierceJaw had been completely overhauled—no, replaced. Every inch of available space had been crammed with a walking-proulsion booster, trading almost all endurance on flat ground for sharper battlefield agility. Stabilizers were bolted to both sides of the feet. \"Jack, what the hell's going on here!?\" Smith snapped. \"One more tweak and the thing will be unrecognizable!\""}, {"title": "Temporary Deployment", "text": "It was too late to restore FierceJaw. During a DLAF emergency operation, all ST units within a 500-kilometer radius were deployed for battle, and all FierceJaws were included on the conscription list. Led by Jack, an entire group of FierceJaw pilots had carried out unauthorized modifications to this model—technically a court-martial offence. These mods transformed FierceJaw from a Heavy ST with strong defense and decent maneuverability into an ST with obvious armor weak points, fit only for combat in specific, complex terrain. \"Great...\" said Smith. \"You're going to get arrested. And now I'm implicated too...\"\"Impossible,\" Jack replied. \"I've entrusted my life to my ST. She won't betray me. She knows I'm fighting for something better.\"", "comment": {"by": "Grant", "text": "Yes, pilots know what they want and know which modification suits them best, unless... they just don't have the money for modifications."}}, {"title": "Combat Feedback", "text": "Five task groups took part in the emergency operation against revived insurgents in the Sutherland region. The first 4 assaults were all pushed back with heavy losses. The returning STs were missing limbs, with wounded pilots shouting for a savior, a hero like the old ace, Rex. Jack had no time to talk. The fifth task group sortied and made light work of the enemy. In this action, the modified FierceJaw used its unique mobility to evade heavy weapons, while relying on heavy-armored sections of its frame to brute-force through enemy fire. After breaching the rebel's defense line and anti-ST trenches, the battle tilted in the DLAF's favor. The full modification plan for FierceJaw ended up being sent to a development institute, leading researchers to re-examine the demands of frontline combat. After a series of further modifications, the FierceJaw we know today was born. It's far from perfect—by some metrics weaker than the old model—but in real-world scenarios, its performance is unquestionable.", "comment": {"by": "Naomi", "text": "It seems that the Sutherland region has become a DLAF training ground, which is not a good thing. Shouldn't the esteemed members of the council perhaps reassess their subversion strategy?"}}]}, "20610103": {"profile": [], "introduction": "SAT-283 萤石\n由希德制造研发的中型机兵，是该厂「宝石」系列的第二款产品，目前主要列装于晨星同盟防卫军远程打击部队。\n作为一款主要负责远程打击的机兵，SAT-283萤石继承了希德制造重视火力与性价比的优良传统。它有计划地降低了高出力引擎、深度武装接口等新锐技术在设计中的比重，大量采用了成熟部件，包括与SAT-331项目相似的模块化装甲和索敌单元，以及经SAT-209G项目后改进的供能供弹组件。此外，SAT-283萤石头部、双肩、躯干等部位搭载了9组高精度火控校准仪，它们与武装、动力模块直接相连，共同组成了可以高效辅助射击的「日蚀火控核心」，使得该型机兵即使在失去精确引导的劣势战场上依然可以实现远程火力压制。尽管正式入列的时间不算长，但它凭借火力与可靠性取得的累累战果已经足够证明其作为战争兵器的价值。"}, "30070103": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "UKB-1"}], "introduction": "HU-08M Gillesrais\nMade by the UKB-1, this heavy ST utilizes a unique Arashium alloy smelting technique, distinct from that used by Obsidian.\nThis proprietary smelting method allows the Arashium to form a unique lattice structure in its inner frame and actuator, greatly enhancing durability and facilitating self-repair capabilities.", "stories": [{"title": "The Sleeping Remains", "text": "During the last war, Dawnstar League lost a Gillesrais. Its wreckage remains in a Port Kadrey research lab. The Gillesrais ST debuted in the Milkhama War, secretly manufactured by UKB-1 for Dawnstar League. The NDF found themselves powerless against it in combat, no ST could face it head-on. They ultimately destroyed it using a custom rail gun trap.", "comment": {"by": "Grant", "text": "Second-rate pilots like us? Gillesrais won't touch us - they hunt the elite."}}, {"title": "Atypical ST", "text": "The Gillesrais: An Unbeatable Mech Beast\nThis legendary heavy ST still dominates the battlefield, defying the evolution of Steel Troopers. Dawnstar League's elite research squad cracked the code behind Gillesrais' enduring supremacy. After relentless investigation, they unlocked the secret of its skeleton: a revolutionary alloy forged through cutting-edge smelting and cooling. The result? A mind-blowing crystal lattice that skyrockets strength and fatigue resistance. Gillesrais reigns supreme, leaving other mechs in the dust!"}, {"title": "An Old Story", "text": "Groundbreaking discovery! Ovett's secret tech crafted Gillesrais with a mysterious Arashium Alloy, defying known Obsidian specs. This revolutionary material propelled Gillesrais to legendary status, outperforming its era. The Gillesrais revival project is now priority. Fusing cutting-edge Steel Trooper tech could birth an epoch-defining heavy ST, ready to dominate the battlefield!"}, {"title": "Operation Restoration", "text": "The Gillesrais Revival Project hits another snag! Tech wizards nailed the mech's outer shell, but the endoskeleton's still not up to snuff. Cracking this robo-riddle's gonna cost big time, so mass production's back on ice. Word on the street? The old Ovid factory's got some skeleton in its closet. Time to unleash the shadow ops and dig deeper!", "comment": {"by": "Yevgeny", "text": "Before the corrupt aristocratic oligarchs seized power, Ovett pulsed with energy and promise. Now? Hah! The vanishing Steel Trooper tech is just the tip of the iceberg in Ovett's downward spiral. A nation's fall, crystallized in lost mecha might."}}]}, "20530103": {"profile": [], "introduction": "DD-264 猎斗士\n由多尔工业与角雕商会联合研发的中型机兵，是专为佣兵设计的新式模块化作战平台。\nDD-264猎斗士将设计的重心牢牢锁定在「实战」这一点上，它采用了经过多次迭代的XF3S规格钢岚合金框架，搭配具有双冗余设计的T型超高压涡轮动力系统，拥有在绝大多数环境下均可稳定运转的扎实基础。全身的模块化装甲接口和通用武器挂点确保了它具有巨大的替换改装空间，使用者既可在战前根据自身风格精细调整武装倾向，也可在战场上快速更换受损部件或切换任务套件。DD-264猎斗士代表的是一种「可预测可负担的革新」，它或许不受机兵评论家青睐，但对追求效率与生存的佣兵而言无疑是最为可靠的战斗兵器。"}, "10140103": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "Doll Industries"}], "introduction": "DD-117 Glasya\nA light melee ST developed by Doll Industries to compete with the Obsidian-produced Dopplesoldner. \nThe front of this ST's body is equipped with Doll Industries' specially customized \"Equilibrium\" assisted locking system, which consists of three coaxial observation scopes and a positioning chip. This system allows a locked ST to remain within Glasya's attack range.\nGlasya had a short development time at Doll Industries and only a limited number were deployed to the frontline. It is said to have been developed by disassembling and studying a captured ST.", "stories": [{"title": "Glasya", "text": "Leaving the arsenal, I enter vast Milkhama. Beneath its peaceful facade, war rages through desert and jungle, city and village. I sense my opponents - perfect to test my combat prowess. United as one, I am the world's finest warrior. My auxiliary targeting system primed, titanium bones and aerospace armor ready. Let them endure my strikes - though I hunger for a true equal.", "comment": {"by": "Naomi", "text": "That's your high-tech toy? A talking ST? Hilarious."}}, {"title": "\"Man\" of Steel", "text": "When pile bunker pierce cockpits, I remember that frail body's dream. Flesh mastered combat, but steel gods demanded more. Doll Industry warned him about Glasya. Price of divine power.", "comment": {"by": "Naomi", "text": "Second Hospital lets patients journal freely. Must be nice. Hey Hong, your intel's here—mostly ravings. Rest is yours to decode."}}, {"title": "Breaking the Shackles", "text": "How long will \"I\" last? Not my call. Martial arts legends scaled these peaks before—all fell to time. But freedom from flesh might keep the legend alive. That's my path.\nInside steel, I move with its stride, strike with its fists. \"I\" fades. Pure martial spirit—that's the peak I chase. Who am I? I am Glasya."}, {"title": "Save the Martial Soul", "text": "My story ends with five Storms surrounding us. I took down three before falling, a feat no other fighter has achieved in Milkhama, past or present. Two Storms remain, but my comrades are gone. I'm leaving behind a fully calibrated Glasya and embracing my fate. The Glasya must survive—it bridges past, present, and future. It won't be destroyed. Another fighter will pilot it, continuing our legacy. Warriors may fall, but our fighting spirit lives on. The Glasya is both a vessel and an extension of our will, eternal as the stars that light our path.", "comment": {"by": "Hong", "text": "An unseen old friend... No need to meet now. I'm in the cockpit—seeing, breathing, fighting. He's already here."}}]}, "10280103": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "An-Holt"}], "introduction": "AST-42HMC Hasteraze\nA Light ST jointly developed by An-Holt Corporation and the Advanced Weapon Research Institute of the Armored Forces.\nServing as a next-generation technology validation platform, it represents an extreme implementation of cutting-edge systems. At its core is the \"Flash Array,\" a multicore micro bionic intelligence framework trained on data from the elite pilot Ada Diaz. Through continuous iteration, it drives the unit's close- to mid-range mobility and melee combat performance to peak levels. This overwhelming capability comes at a cost—both financial and physiological. Its operational demands are lethal to unqualified pilots. Despite extensive optimization efforts by the DLAF, only one unit remains in active service.", "stories": [{"title": "Arms Race", "text": "Through the border war, the DL secured its position on Milkhama Island and achieved its strategic goals. But the heavy losses also alarmed the Defense Forces. They could not afford to fall behind in mech technology or combat systems. In XC 105, a next-generation tech demonstrator program was quietly launched, with major research institutes and partner defense companies invited to compete.\nAfter two years of selection, only An-Holt and the Defense Forces' Advanced Weapons Research Institute remained. Both proposals met the military's future combat vision. Just as a decision was pending, new intelligence arrived—the UNCS and Obsidian had already entered component testing for a new mech using Dr. Walter Newman's Nova Frame, with performance exceeding third-generation standards. The DL was forced to reassess the program timeline."}, {"title": "Joint Development", "text": "To push the program forward, the DL required An-Holt and the Advanced Weapons Research Institute to merge their designs and jointly develop a next-generation mech capable of matching or surpassing the UNCS prototype across all key metrics. The Oceanic Conclave approved a major increase in funding and deployed additional experts to support the effort. Even so, integrating different design approaches with cutting-edge technology proved extremely challenging.\nAfter three more years of development, the first prototype finally entered trial operation, but its performance fell short. Heavy reliance on unproven technologies led to poor stability, while sacrificing performance for reliability would defeat the project's purpose.\n\"We've hit a dead end. Without a breakthrough like the Nova Frame, this project isn't going anywhere.\""}, {"title": "Turnaround", "text": "Breakthroughs often come from the unexpected. Dr. Walter Newman secretly reached out to the DL, attempting to defect to East Milkhama with Hyper-Aptamer data. Although the plan ultimately failed, part of the data—and a young Ada Diaz—were secured. From that point on, the long-stalled next-gen program began moving again.\nThe incomplete Hyper-Aptamer data couldn't be applied directly, but it sparked a key breakthrough. Dr. Elise used it to rebuild a practical bionic intelligence framework, opening a new path distinct from the UNCS. Based on this, the Advanced Weapons Research Institute developed a new computational module, easing the conflict between stability and performance.\nAt the same time, Ada Diaz's exceptional reaction speed and control precision impressed both the design team and the military. With her as the test pilot, even the prototype's current limits began to look conservative."}, {"title": "Ace", "text": "Advances in Arashium Alloy applications, miniaturized military bionic frameworks, and the successful test run of the Arashi self-circulating engine all stemmed from the next-gen mech program, driving rapid progress across multiple fields. These breakthroughs in turn fed back into the project, allowing continuous upgrades to the prototype. In July, XC 115, optimization was completed and the AST-42HMC was finalized. The new unit was delivered, passed military acceptance, and was officially named \"Hasteraze,\" while the original prototype was archived.\nDue to extended testing, Hasteraze's combat OS became tightly bound to Ada Diaz. Even well-trained elite pilots could not replicate her performance, and its extreme cost made mass production impossible. In the end, the DL did not obtain a general-purpose validation unit, but achieved a major breakthrough in high-performance systems. With Ada and Hasteraze deployed together, victory was almost guaranteed.", "comment": {"by": "Matilda", "text": "I had a brief hand in testing and refining the Hasteraze prototype. It really was something else… a machine like that almost feels unreal. Still, putting the outcome of a fight on a young girl's shoulders is a dangerous call, no matter how you look at it."}}]}, "10380103": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "Kamadar"}], "introduction": "KX-099HM Hector\nA third-generation Light ST manufactured by Kamadar, favored by special forces from multiple countries for its outstanding maneuverability in combat.\nAs the company's first independently developed high-end Light ST, the KX-099HM Hector effectively fills the gap in Kamadar's product line for high-mobility, strong-attack models. The new arashium alloy framework and sensor monitoring module, improved from the KX-098 Odysseus, combined with a miniaturized high-power propulsion system, allow the Hector to exceed the standard level of third-generation Light STs in terms of protection and mobility. Additionally, the Defiant Units installed at each joint are directly connected to the propulsion system, enabling partial energy recovery from emergency maneuvers and short-term storage, which is then released through the Armed System to achieve highly aggressive tactical counterattacks.", "stories": [{"title": "A Difficult Start", "text": "In XC 113, Kamadar launched its next-generation mech development program, outlining seven parallel R&D tracks—one of which was the high-end light mech project KX-099HM, codenamed \"Hector.\" Like the KX-098 Odysseus project initiated alongside it, Hector inherited the battlefield anchor role established by the KX-075 Heracles, while placing greater emphasis on counteroffensive capability to support localized battlefield suppression in future joint deployments. However, unlike its experience with medium and heavy platforms, Kamadar had no prior track record in developing high-end light mechs. As a result, the project ran into significant issues early on during the concept validation and simulation phase, with internal disagreements preventing the team from reaching a unified direction. This deadlock persisted for nearly five months, until a major breakthrough by Kamadar's power systems division in March, XC 114 finally enabled the team to lock in a definitive design path."}, {"title": "Advanced Prototype", "text": "After evaluating its projected combat performance, the team scrapped the original concept of a high-mobility, mid-to-long-range fire support unit. Instead, they shifted focus toward maximizing battlefield control and immediate counterattack capability, defining the KX-099HM Hector as a close-range combat platform. With key breakthroughs from R&D, Hector was able to integrate a next-generation Arashium Alloy frame, advanced sensor modules, and a compact high-output propulsion system, pushing both protection and mobility well beyond standard light mech benchmarks. Once the project entered the prototype production phase, Kamadar's strong manufacturing capacity and precision assembly capabilities proved critical, allowing most new components to be produced and tuned in a short time. Barring any unexpected setbacks, the KX-099HM prototype would soon complete full assembly and move into extreme performance testing."}, {"title": "Core Neuron", "text": "In July, XC 116, the first KX-099HM prototype entered live combat testing, but the results fell short of expectations. Its mobility performed as intended, allowing for sustained operations in high-intensity environments, but the conservative weapon loadout limited its offensive output—even in extended engagements, it struggled to deliver decisive results. Attempts to upgrade its armament led to balance issues and reduced mobility, running counter to the platform's original design philosophy and forcing the team to explore alternative solutions. The breakthrough came from an unexpected source—kinetic energy recovery systems used in racing vehicles. By integrating a network of micro energy storage units across the mech's joints and linking them directly to the power system, excess energy generated during high-load maneuvers could be captured and briefly stored, then released through the weapon systems. This significantly increased offensive output without adding to overall energy consumption. Known as the \"Defiant Unit,\" this innovation finally enabled the KX-099HM to execute the aggressive breakthrough and counteroffensive tactics it was designed for."}, {"title": "Significant Headway", "text": "The upgraded KX-099HM Hector delivered strong results across multiple field tests, quickly drawing attention from a wide range of players—military procurement offices, elite mercenary groups, and major trade organizations all sent teams to evaluate it. Kamadar moved fast to capitalize, expanding its presence in the high-end light mech market by leasing early production units at reduced rates and deploying technical staff to support on-site testing and tuning, ensuring the platform met client requirements. The strategy paid off, around 70% of target customers committed to procurement, including elite units such as the UNCS Maneuver Battalion and the DL Oversight Committee. Ongoing partnerships with these forces also generated extensive combat data and frontline pilot feedback, giving Kamadar a valuable edge in light mech development. Several military analysts believe the platform's success marks a major step forward for Kamadar, positioning it firmly among the leading developers of next-generation units."}]}, "10350103": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "Obsidian"}], "introduction": "OS-13S Hela\nA light ST designed by the Cicero Laboratory and workshopped by Obsidian before production.\nThis model was specially designed for Predators, and is optimized for enhanced mobility and survival capabilities.\nThe cockpit of the Hela is equipped with a \"Garm Unit\" that can collect information on the battlefield. In certain situations this unit can facilitate increased pilot-ST integration.", "stories": [{"title": "Sharing Agreement", "text": "\"Based on the three-year tech sharing agreement between Obsidian and yourself, we require the transfer of ST Hela's manufacturing specs, along with your support for production. To Dr. Cicero.\" As you read aloud, you watch Cicero's face—first shock, then distress, finally acceptance. Everything proceeds as planned. As Obsidian's liaison, you secured Hela's ST designs upon departing his lab. As expected."}, {"title": "High-end Optimization", "text": "The Obsidian Lab's no backwater operation. It's a nexus of cutting-edge tech and top-tier talent, primed to scrutinize Hela's blueprint with laser precision. Sure, Hela's design's got some kinks, but nothing a few tweaks can't iron out.\nYou spot the eggheads scrapping the Garm device. It's Bloodfang's pricey offspring, jacking up instability without payoff. But they're keeping the pilot enhancement system. Obsidian's got ace pilots, but you can never have too much muscle in the cockpit.\nAs Obsidian's Hela hits the combat trials, Cicero rings you up. The doc's sweating bullets, harping on about keeping the Garm device. Claims it's Hela's beating heart.\nNobody's buying it. After all, the mech's creator isn't always its master."}, {"title": "Stronger to Strongest", "text": "Obsidian's mecha showdown: New Hela vs. Original!\nEpic clash of titans as skilled pilots face off in combat trials.\nNew Hela triumphs in fierce battle, but victory turns to chaos.\nRogue mecha goes berserk, forcing Obsidian to terminate with extreme prejudice.\nShocking revelation: Pilot's body ravaged by prototype enhancer, mind lost to madness."}, {"title": "Renewed", "text": "\"Think everyone's like that Predator Squad madwoman?\" Cicero shouts through the phone. \"This ST was built for a Hyper-Aptamer! Who else can handle that drug load?\" As Obsidian's liaison, you can't agree, not with senior researchers watching. You document Cicero's revisions: strip most pilot enhancement systems, retain the costlier Garm device. When you next see Hela, the ST is vastly improved, no longer harmful to pilots. But open that cockpit, examine deeper, and you'll find ghosts of the original design—dense webs of drug delivery tubes and dead cortical electrodes.", "comment": {"by": "Naomi", "text": "Meet the Hela: our battlefield nemesis. Stay alert! A few tweaks, and this mech beast could pack an even meaner punch. Remember, test subjects are expendable in this brutal mecha war."}}]}, "30060103": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "Kamadar"}], "introduction": "KX-075 Heracles\nMade by Kamadar, this heavy ST is a modified version of the first high-end SL to utilize Arashium alloy.\nModifications, intended to enhance military effectiveness, include increased load capacity and high-power output characteristics. A miniaturized vibration jammer has been installed on this ST to suppress target vibration, reducing the enemy's dodge rate.", "stories": [{"title": "Engineering Prototype", "text": "The Heracles prototype emerged from Milkhama's early Engineering STs, pioneering the use of Arashium Alloy. Built for logging and mining, it boasted a robust transmission and potent power system. When its load-bearing capacity was redirected to weaponry and armor, this towering mech transformed into a formidable war machine."}, {"title": "Military Modification", "text": "Kamadar spearheads Project Heracles, the ultimate mech upgrade. Top brass brought in cutting-edge Obsidian tech to supercharge this war machine. Pushing Heracles beyond its limits, Kamadar unlocked next-gen signal jamming and suppression capabilities. The Arashium Alloy Actuator got a serious boost, and they crammed a compact interference terminal into Heracles' colossal frame. Flip the switch, and nearby targets feel the heat. This beast is ready to dominate the battlefield!"}, {"title": "Core Technology", "text": "Heracles' signal jamming and suppression tech proved stellar in trials, pushing Kamadar to max out its potential. Upgrades focused on boosting range, power, and precision. To dominate shifting combat zones, Kamadar kitted Heracles with interference amps and wave scanners for adaptable deployment. These mods transformed Heracles from a mere Engineering ST into a devastating war machine, ready to wreak havoc on the battlefield."}, {"title": "Industrial Support", "text": "The Heracles mech dominated the NDF Exercise in 111. After DLAF's stealthy Steel Trooper deployment, Heracles became the ultimate fire magnet. Enemy mobile units crumbled under its overwhelming suppression. Allied forces, backed by Heracles' cover, swiftly captured key positions. The mech's jaw-dropping performance caught every faction's eye, but its sky-high price tag limited orders to a select few from DLAF and NDF.", "comment": {"by": "Grant", "text": "Pricey? Sure. But this heavy-duty Arashium ST is the real deal! No bargain-bin bot can handle what Heracles dishes out!"}}]}, "33020103": {"profile": [], "introduction": "DMS-000 辉龙\n由温斯顿博士设计，拉尼亚凯亚制造的重型机兵。该机整合了全钢岚合金框架、机械与脑波复合驱动系统等新技术，拥有优秀的基础性能。在受到异世界龙神加护之后，它的外形和操作模式发生了进一步变化。"}, "20420103": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "SEED"}], "introduction": "SAT-209 Igniter\nA Medium ST developed by SEED Manufacturing.\nIt features a dual-antenna head design and a back interface compatible with various ammo types, along with asymmetric leg armor. The Igniter is a true one-man tactical unit, capable of independently completing long-range strike locking and guidance without relying on other reconnaissance or intel support. Its \"Lumiflow\" core provides faster and more powerful boosts for ultra-long-range tactical weapons.", "stories": [{"title": "Market Upheaval", "text": "\"Since the end of the border war, Tactical STs designed primarily for missile and rocket payloads have faced a long winter in the marketplace. The main drivers of this decline are shrinking demand and operational scenarios, compounded by the barrier-to-entry posed by modern satellite navigation systems. Today, the situation in Milkhama has shifted into a stage dominated by two superpowers, with frequent small-scale conflicts. Without access to the reconnaissance networks of either bloc, the tactical applications for such STs are severely limited. Unless you possess the kind of overwhelming resources and influence that Obsidian commands, enough to build your own tactical satellite network to support your products... there's simply no justification for developing next-gen Tactical STs.\" — Milkhama ST Observations VOL.77", "comment": {"by": "Arthur", "text": "The first floor is mine!"}}, {"title": "Distinct Design", "text": "\"We can hardlyimagine what kind of Tactical ST would be expected to carryout a missile strike entirely on its own, without any other intelligence. As everyone knows, warfare is—and always has been—the art of coordination between different units and departments. This is especially true for tactical weapons like missiles and rockets. Currently, market-proven Tactical STs are all doubling down on interoperability with auxiliary support systems. Yet SEED seems intent on defying these principles. They are attempting to develop a single-pilot Tactical ST capable of independently conducting reconnaissance, targeting, and guidance—no reliance on satellites, ground-based guidance, anything. Handling every stage of the strike solo. Admittedly, this does fit SEED's niche: finding some unorthodox angle, carving out a brand-new, potentially lucrative market for themselves. But ultimately, due to their limited R&D resources, they end up competing mostly in the \"bang for buck\" category...\" — Milkhama ST Observations VOL.89", "comment": {"by": "Arthur", "text": "This design is absolute genius! Only SEED truly understands what their pilots face and the type of ST they need! Not all pilots have the support of tactical satellites and reconnaissance drones. The ability to perform these tasks solo makes these Tactical STs so incredible."}}, {"title": "Research and Development Difficulties", "text": "\"As previously leaked, the SEED Autonomous Tactical ST is currently facing a development bottleneck. In the past, SEED has always managed to steer things back on track and get the product to market. This time, however, their luck may have run out. According to relevant data, the production of the SAT-209 has been thrown into crisis by a break in the upstream supply chain. SEED has no cost advantage on several key components, and multiple suppliers—bound by exclusive contracts with rival manufacturers—have refused to support SEED's products. Taking all this and the market situation into account, it's not hard to conclude that the SAT-209 will face serious challenges. The stalled production may well be the price SEED is paying for its own aggressive strategic bets.\" — Milkhama ST Observations VOL.115", "comment": {"by": "Arthur", "text": "I've gotten used to it—every time, they make their entrance under a cloud of doubt and smear campaigns, only to stun the world once again. Because SEED pours every bit of funding into research and manufacturing, not into hiring online shills or paying media outlets to stir up hype..."}}, {"title": "Igniter", "text": "\"...Ultimately, the SAT-209, a Medium Tactical ST known commercially as Igniter, launched amid a barrage of bad press and criticism. Although it still showcases SEED's signature traits—ultra-low pricing, an exhaustive accessory suite, and fantastic value for money—its atrocious compatibility and system optimization remain hard to fathom. It's unlikely that either the UNCS nor the DL will include Igniter in their procurement plans. Other military organizations and mercenary outfits will likewise remain cautious. Igniter's main audience will only be those Mercenaries active in conflict zones, or terrorists... Of course, for them, Igniter is the closest thing to a flagship product they can afford.\" — Milkhama ST Observations VOL.139", "comment": {"by": "Arthur", "text": "[This comment has been hidden. The user has been banned for 30 days due to excessive or inflammatory remarks.]"}}]}, "10360103": {"profile": [], "introduction": "HU-41E 幻惑\n联合设计局全新研发的轻型机兵，目前仍处于实战验证阶段，尚未成规模列装。\n该机型完全采用奥维特技术打造，不仅拥有独特的外形，其内部的钢岚合金框架、模块连接结构、动力单元乃至主控系统更是与米赫玛岛上的其他机兵有着不小的差别。这种非常规的设计使得HU-41E拥有优秀的基础性能，且可实现非常规的武装搭配，但这同时也意味着只有足够优秀的整备员与机师才能发挥其真正的作战能力。"}, "30200103": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "Katana"}], "introduction": "ART-108 Dragon's True Blade, Export Name: Kagemusha\nA heavy ST jointly developed by Katana and renowned ST designer Masamune Shinohara.\nART-108 retains Shinohara's distinctive personal style, featuring a refined structural design in its exterior armor that balances its stylized appearance with the unique high protection capabilities of Heavy STs. The \"Zanshin\" Chip installed in the torso can adjust power output based on real-time combat conditions. Its formidable continuous combat effectiveness makes the Kagemusha a true battlefield behemoth.", "stories": [{"title": "Far East Deployment", "text": "As the discovery site of arashi matter, Milkhama Island has served as the center of ST R&D and arashi industry since the Border War. Shaped by geopolitical conflict and mercenary warfare, the island became a paradise for arashium STs. Nearly every major ST manufacturer established industrial parks or branch facilities there, drawing elite pilots and technical talent from across the world. Yet excellence is not exclusive to Milkhama. Other regions continue to produce outstanding ST manufacturers and designers. Among them, the emerging ST manufacturer Katana identified overseas markets as fertile ground, establishing its ST industry footprint early in the Far East."}, {"title": "Dragon's True Blade", "text": "As the headquarters of Katana, the Ryuzen region in the Far East boasts a strong heavy industry foundation and talented ST designers. Masamune Shinohara, a star designer who has won awards at the Milthus ST exhibition, joined Katana at the invitation of its founder, Raphael Gideon, to lead the design and development of Katana's ART series STs. The first work Masamune Shinohara brought to Katana was the Heavy ST ART-108, positioned as a frontline battlefield ST and designed with elements of Far Eastern warriors.", "comment": {"by": "Naomi", "text": "Those Far Easterners have long been involved in the situation on Milkhama Island. The two members of the Shinohara family are perfect examples... I mean, how could a Far Easterner just randomly end up on Milkhama Island and get involved in the Hyper-Aptamer Experiment... So the Shinohara family has been designing STs since the Border War period? Impressive!"}}, {"title": "Unorthodox Channels", "text": "According to the naming tradition of the Ryuzen region, ART-108 was named Dragon's True Blade, with the full name being Shinohara's True Dragon Blade of Ryuzen. Although Katana believed that such a name sufficiently showcased the manufacturer's style and regional characteristics, ART-108 was renamed Kagemusha at the suggestion of Shinohara himself and was marketed as a cutting-edge concept machine. Perhaps due to concerns about the increasingly complex situation on Milkhama Island, Katana did not participate in the launch and sale of ART-108 in the Milkhama region. Instead, it was sold through the Harpy Guild as an agent distributor in the Milkhama region."}, {"title": "Offshore Strategy", "text": "Due to the unique nature of its release channels, the detailed sales data of the Kagemusha remains unknown to the public. Given Katana's consistent high-end and cutting-edge product positioning, the price of ART-108 is significantly higher than common models with similar positioning. The overly distinctive personal style of its design has resulted in the Kagemusha having few followers among mercenaries who prioritize practicality. Surprisingly, the Kagemusha has achieved remarkable success outside of Milkhama. It has even achieved good sales in the homeland of the two superpowers and the Principality of Ovett. With the release of the Kagemusha, rumors have begun to circulate in the ST market about traditional mech manufacturers planning to expand beyond Milkhama. Perhaps in the near future, the ST market outside of Milkhama will increasingly attract the attention of manufacturers, and the ST field will usher in a new round of reshuffling.", "comment": {"by": "Grant", "text": "Ha, what do those outsiders know about Milkhama? These flashy models get blown to bits in no time... Who'd wanna spend that much money just to become a sitting duck on the battlefield?"}}]}, "30170103": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "Laniakea"}], "introduction": "LTX-305R Kong\nA heavy ST produced by Laniakea for elite NDF units only.\nEach part of the ST is equipped with an energy storage hub to enhance its suppressive firepower. It can reuse energy generated by its weapons, allowing it to maximize striking power. Its suspension frame includes a custom heavy weapon adapter module, making it ideal for battlefield environments where high firepower is required.", "stories": [{"title": "Cutting-Edge Type", "text": "Laniakea's apex assault mech boasts a cutting-edge energy transfer system. This beast can lock down fire zones with its robust defenses, then unleash hell with its heavy artillery. A true battlefield dominator. In solo ops, it's a force to be reckoned with. For critical missions, it's backed by Aurora support units. Give this monster room to breathe, and it'll rain down destruction like you've never seen."}, {"title": "Energy Storage Transfer", "text": "The Kong's Energy Storage Hub rapidly channels massive power to its weapon systems. Perfectly compatible with heavy armaments like the Ifrit, Wrath of Mars, and Dragonbreath, this ST delivers firepower that outclasses other mechs. In combat, the Kong deploys to strategic positions, using its robust defenses and devastating output to suppress enemy fire and shield allied forces."}, {"title": "Active Promoter", "text": "After development, Kong underwent evaluation by the UNCS Elite Force. A simulated battle with 20 ace pilots would determine the mech's combat potential, with the sole survivor given authority for final assessment. As the victor's cockpit opened, spectators gasped—Viceroy Blair himself sat within. The Viceroy praised Kong's performance and requested a unit for his command. Following this event, UNCS ST pilot training standards were elevated. The pilots shared renewed optimism about both warfare and the NDF's future.", "comment": {"by": "Marcus", "text": "When your general's a warrior, not some desk jockey—that's when you charge."}}, {"title": "Light Capacity", "text": "Of the 35 Kong STs scheduled for Q2 delivery, only 7 units were completed, with the Viceroy claiming 2. Production faced minor setbacks from funding shortages and equipment import restrictions. Military budget prioritized city defenses and combat zone upgrades, while new production gear remained stuck in customs. Due to these limitations, Kong STs were issued exclusively to select UNCS elite units.", "comment": {"by": "Marcus", "text": "Crank out a dozen Steel Troopers in a crane shop? No sweat. But the military's mecha assembly line? That's a whole different beast. Precision, power, and protocols set it leagues apart from civilian operations."}}]}, "20170103": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "Obsidian"}], "introduction": "YOS-99 Malthus\nA medium-class tactical mech developed by Obsidian, purpose-built for large-scale battles and primarily deployed across Obsidian's various private military forces.\nDeveloped in parallel with the OS-77 Wolverine, the Malthus emphasizes wide-area firepower over the Wolverine's focus on small-unit strikes. Enhanced rocket and missile saturation capabilities grant it outstanding long-range area denial, enabling significant firepower output in large engagements and paving the way for successful offensive and defensive operations at the tactical level.", "stories": [{"title": "Stock Unfreezing", "text": "Malthus: the mech that almost never was. Shelved by Obsidian after failing to find its niche, this powerhouse has risen from the ashes. Boasting enhanced rocket coverage, Malthus unleashes devastating firepower in massive engagements. A tactical juggernaut, it's equally adept at defense and offense. Time to show the battlefield what it's been missing!"}, {"title": "Firepower Duo", "text": "The Malthus mech, dusting off its warehouse cobwebs, roars back to life thanks to the Wolverine's combat triumphs!\nObsidian's latest firepower duo packs a punch: The Wolverine, a precision striker, and the Malthus, a zone devastator. These mechs are the perfect tag team for tomorrow's battlefields. With Wolverines flying off the shelves, Obsidian's crafting its own long-range legion. The Malthus assembly lines are firing up again!"}, {"title": "First Try", "text": "Malthus mecha debuts in epic Milthus City siege! Northern sector bombarded by mystery hostiles, city defenders execute tactical retreat. Lured attackers into exposed wasteland trap.\nRecon STs and orbital eyes feed Malthus units pinpoint intel. 15 Malthus mechs unleash 700+ rocket salvos in 24 hours! Obliterate enemy artillery nests and vaporize two supply convoys. Malthus firepower halts invaders' advance on Milthus City."}, {"title": "Changes and Competitions", "text": "Post-war shakeups left Malthus mechs pilotless. New recruits face grueling adaptation training.\nModified Malthus units hit the global market. When grilled about WMD proliferation risks, Milthus brass assured: \"Every buyer undergoes rigorous vetting. Safety's our top priority.\"", "comment": {"by": "Grant", "text": "The top mech jockeys are flocking to Milthus City for prime gigs. ST operators are a dying breed these days. Better move fast if you want in on the action!"}}]}, "30100103": {"profile": [], "introduction": "YOS-95A 殉道士\n黑曜石开发的新式重型机兵，目前仅少量列装于黑曜石机动警卫队。\n该型机兵采用了黑曜石全新改进的XF4R钢岚合金框架及电磁复合装甲，拥有极为可靠的生存能力；双臂多达32组传感器均直接连接火控、动力与操纵模块，即使在高负荷战斗下依然可以瞬时辅助机师调整机体姿态。此外，黑曜石还为其开发了能引起小范围内敌我机兵钢岚合金振动的「荆棘回路」，于战斗瞬时增幅自身的输出功率和结构强度，从而显著提升机动奔袭与近身格斗的作战效能——但同时，它也会给驾驶者带来巨大的操控压力和神经刺激，只有不知恐惧的傀儡或意志坚定的战士才能真正发挥其全部实力。"}, "20500103": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "An-Holt"}], "introduction": "AST-07 Mithril\nAn-Holt Corporation's new medium tactical model surpasses its predecessor, Hermes, with enhanced performance, armor, and equipment.\nEquipped with the latest Arashium drive core and optimized for next-gen tactical weapons, it offers premium battlefield adaptability, and the onboard Supercomputer Type-R provides advanced enemy analysis. Rumor has it that the Mithril once housed a [Dive] connection device, indicating it was once a specialized ST project for a unique pilot.", "stories": [{"title": "Transmission Code A", "text": "\"We have achieved an unshakable lead in the field of tactical STs. The AST-06 boasts the highest production, sales, profits, and market share... Any tactical pilot worth their salt will choose the Hermes—all tactical strike forces will be equipped with the Hermes... Our next development direction should be to tap into the existing user base further and maintain products centered around the Hermes... instead of investing heavily in developing so-called next-generation cutting-edge tactical STs... The Milkhama War ended fifteen years ago, and the era of peace era no longer requires more extreme tactical STs... We, all of us, must be prepared to enter a new era.\"", "comment": {"by": "Shawnee", "text": "Following the Milkhama War, ST manufacturers faced confusion and downsized production lines, leading to an influx of technical personnel and STs into the black market. This exacerbated the chaos in Milkhama."}}, {"title": "Transmission Code H", "text": "\"I saw her, I did! She's not even a seasoned investor, just a little girl... No, not the one Doll, the one with long white hair... I heard the chief personally showed her all over the 07 research institute and factory—they even went to the firepower testing ground... Sure, there have been rumors that they're about to restart AST-07 research, but no investor would be crazy enough to invest in a project with zero chance of success. Well, she looks inexperienced and outright crazy... Uh, no, I didn't say anything bad about our new investor! Our whole team is grateful to her! Whether we can keep our jobs or not all depends on her!\"", "comment": {"by": "Alyson", "text": "Next time, wear Doll's emblem. It'll save you from judgy people. Seriously."}}, {"title": "Transmission Code W", "text": "\"It's already been confirmed—she's a Hyper-Aptamer who escaped from one of those labs. What a world! It's amazing how An-Holt even has a chance to get close to something only super manufacturers like Obsidian and Laniakea can access. We're not the only ones interested in her—those DL guys have gotten wind of it, too, and they've been in private contact with us. If we can take advantage of this situation and get the resources and intelligence we need from both the superpowers, An-Holt's rise to power won't be too far behind. I just hope the price for all this won't be too high...\"", "comment": {"by": "Cicero", "text": "Hehe... Based on my experience, the DL wouldn't deploy troops merely for the capture of one or two Hyper-Aptamers. This suggests they're likely aiming for a new target of considerable value."}}, {"title": "Transmission Code Z", "text": "\"The AST-07 project will continue to search for potential pilots, and even if it doesn't find the perfect match, its capabilities as a tactical ST surpass those of any other ST on the market. This is due to our technological advancements, exemplified by the AST-06, also developed by An-Holt. Rest assured, the version presented to the public will not be the one you selected, and all support equipment related to the Hyper-Aptamer experiments has been removed. The unit delivered to you will be the authentic [Mithril]. Furthermore, I have obtained updates regarding the 19th production line, including information and technology. The Supercomputer Type-R installed in this unit is from that line. If you are interested, I can provide more details, but it will take some time.\""}]}, "20570103": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "An-Holt"}], "introduction": "AST-74X Nightglow\nA medium ST jointly developed by An-Holt Corporation and Obsidian, it is also another achievement of the Dawnstar League's fourth-generation ST technology validation project.\nDesigned to counter super pilots, the AST-74X incorporates cutting-edge technologies, including an XF4-spec arashium alloy frame, composite armor with a micro shield generator, and an Aura cycle engine with astonishing output power. These technologies give it a clear advantage in basic performance over third-generation STs. Additionally, the active Electromagnetic Introducer and Bionic Intelligence Frame form the Nebula System, distributed throughout the body, enabling semi-autonomous optimization of weapon resource allocation. This grants it a revolutionary tactical edge: even without Hyper-Aptamer pilots or brainwave control systems, it can efficiently operate remote unmanned attack units similar to the Erinys.", "stories": [{"title": "Gray Target", "text": "In XC 115, the next-generation tech demonstrator AST-42HMC Hasteraze, jointly developed by An-Holt and the Defense Forces' Advanced Weapons Research Institute, officially passed military acceptance. Under Ada Diaz's control, its peak performance impressed the armed forces—but also raised concerns within the Oceanic Conclave. If a super pilot equipped with advanced units were to turn against them, the lack of effective countermeasures would leave the Conclave at a serious disadvantage. For that reason, a series of counter–super pilot doctrines were drafted in secrecy, with the AST-74X project—jointly developed by An-Holt and Obsidian—serving as a key component. From the outset, the program aimed to allow a small number of elite units to suppress super pilots. The joint development team drew heavily from Hasteraze and XR test data, and after three months of simulation and validation, established a set of performance parameters that met the design goals. Based on these benchmarks, customized trial production of AST-74X prototype components began."}, {"title": "Critical Data", "text": "In June, XC 117, development of the AST-74X prototype components was largely complete, and the project moved into integration and system calibration. However, the joint development team soon ran into a major issue—the DL's existing mech systems couldn't support the platform's aggressive performance output. A new OS had to be developed alongside the AST-74X, one that could be handled by elite non–Hyper-Aptamer pilots while still fully unlocking the unit's capabilities. Progress slowed due to a lack of usable pilot data, prompting direct intervention from the Oceanic Conclave. In August, a mysterious one-eyed man arrived at the research facility with critical data and joined as a temporary test pilot, taking part in key trials such as engine output modes and composite dynamic fire control. Within just one month, he helped establish a pilot data model that met operational requirements, bringing OS development back on track. Only after he left on another assignment did the team learn his true identity—Colin Doyle, a former Defense Forces ace who had distinguished himself during the Milkhama War."}, {"title": "Test Armament", "text": "In December, XC 117, the AST-74X prototype completed baseline integration and system calibration. Its XF4-grade arashium alloy frame, Composite Armor with a micro shield generator, and the high-output Arashi Cycle Engine all performed reliably under the new OS, pushing its baseline performance well beyond standard third-generation units. However, raw performance alone does not define overall combat capability—its armament is just as critical. The original loadout, a large-caliber rail gun and a micro missile bay, performed well against conventional targets, but fell short in stress tests against super-tier pilots. To address this, Obsidian's designers proposed adopting a new experimental wireless remote drone weapon, commonly referred to as \"Cutter,\" designed to fully leverage the AST-74X's superior output and fire control precision."}, {"title": "Brand New Mode", "text": "The DL's Oceanic Conclave has approved the AST-74X's integration of a new wireless remote drone weapon system, and authorized the Defense Forces' Advanced Weapons Research Institute to supply An-Holt with PAMS-equipped computing modules to further improve the new OS. At the same time, the joint development team carried out another round of modifications to the AST-74X frame, adding multiple active electromagnetic guidance units without compromising balance or overall mobility. These systems enable real-time battlefield data collection and allow the OS to precisely control Arashium Alloy deformation, even autonomously directing remote weapons during high-mobility operations. This parallel, high-intelligence control model removes the need for Hyper-Aptamer pilots. While the added systems significantly increase power consumption, reducing effective combat time below third-generation standards. However, its battlefield dominance outweighs this drawback. In the hands of elite pilots, the platform is expected to achieve its intended doctrine: using a small number of elite units to suppress even top-tier pilots."}]}, "20490103": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "Kamadar"}], "introduction": "KX-098 Odysseus\nA Medium ST manufactured by Kamadar, belonging to the same series as the KX-075 Heracles Heavy ST.\nOdysseus inherits the KX-075's advanced information sensor system, as well as its superior arashium alloy framework. Fine-tuned around the layout of its repair unit, its kinetic monitor formulates support strategies based on the target ST's condition, turning Odysseus into a true battlefield energy hub.", "stories": [{"title": "KX-001", "text": "In the market and among most Pilots, Kamadar has always been perceived as a low-key manufacturer. It maintains a subtle presence in product promotion and takes a modest, pragmatic approach to iteration. Kamadar shares the same locational and labor cost advantages as SEED, yet it has never got as much media coverage. This low profile has even led people to forget that it is a world-leading ST manufacturer with top-notch legs part technology and is also one of the manufacturers with a significant advantage in onboard sensors.", "comment": {"by": "Grant", "text": "Ridiculous statements like that can only come from people who are utterly clueless about STs. Anyone with any familiarity knows that Kamadar is the largest transmission structure contractor and supplier in the industry."}}, {"title": "KX-075", "text": "The last ST launched by Kamadar with significant public influence dates back to the KX-075, commercially known as Heracles. However, due to its early release date, high cost, and low production, Heracles' market presence was less than satisfactory. After the KX-075, Kamadar's new ST development plans stalled. The company shifted its primary business to the subcontracting of Arashium ST transmission systems and the production of related parts. Despite several older ST models from Kamadar still performing well in the market and maintaining a good reputation among most pilots and mercenaries, Kamadar has not announced any new ST development plans since Heracles. Just as many media outlets speculated that Kamadar was exiting the finished ST market to focus on parts manufacturing and supply fields, Kamadar announced the all-new Medium ST \"Odysseus\" in October, XC 118."}, {"title": "KX-098", "text": "For the \"Odysseus,\" its new ST, Kamadar has maintained its usual low-key promotion. There was neither a press conference nor much advertising. Only the official website quietly published the new product introduction and parameter details. However, after thoroughly reviewing this public information, both senior pilots and ST industry media have to feel that this is a product only Kamadar could launch. As an ST with a repair and support role, \"Odysseus\" is equipped with a \"Kinetic Monitor\" that can only be found in Kamadar's factory, bringing kinetic optimization and support modification work from the workshop to the battlefield. At the same time, \"Odysseus\" is also equipped with the signal interference and support systems inherited from previous models, effectively increasing the survival rate and battlefield suitability of other STs around it.", "comment": {"by": "Naomi", "text": "I heard that the higher-ups have procured several 'Odysseus' units for our department... Are they expecting me to operate these clumsy Tactical Assist STs? I know nothing about mechanical repairs or modifications!"}}, {"title": "KX-100", "text": "Whether in terms of the functionality of the ST or its own quality, \"Odysseus\" fully meets the standards of top-tier STs on the current market. Especially with Kamadar's decade-long experience in Arashium Legs technology, \"Odysseus\" has become a unique strategic support specialist. It is reported that besides \"Odysseus,\" Kamadar is also developing a new test machine codenamed KX-100. Informed sources suspect that KX-100 is likely to be the same series ST as the previously leaked \"Odysseus\" and \"Heracles,\" and will be known as \"Achilles.\" However, other reports suggest that the development of KX-100 is still in the early stages, and \"Odysseus\" serves as a stepping stone for its future Research and Development Stage.", "comment": {"by": "Alyson", "text": "In this day and age, 'not hyping' is a form of hype itself... Look, here comes the marketing strategy."}}]}, "10270103": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "Laniakea"}], "introduction": "NED-03 Ouroboros\nA Light ST born in the Laniakea Ursprung Laboratory, the third unit in the NED production line, and the latest Ursprung-type ST.\nSimilar to the first two Ursprung-type STs, Ouroboros is equipped with a modified Nova-Frame and Immaculateur, featuring the most advanced Dive and control technologies, offering extremely high operational limits and piloting thresholds. It exhibits a significant generational leap compared to other models produced by the same manufacturer, especially in terms of Dive sync ratio and instantaneous acceleration, making it a true third-generation arashium ST.", "stories": [{"title": "The Origin", "text": "After the border war, Laniakea made significant advancements in ST technology and Arashium applications, initiating more advanced ST R&D strategies. This coincided with Blair Bluecher's promotion to Governor of the West Milkhama district. His spearheading of ST Research and Hyper-Aptamer experimentation vastly expanded the horizons of Arashium STs technology. The long-dormant Ursprung Laboratory was also reactivated, tasked once more with working on the \"Ursprung\" and \"Testee\"-type units.", "comment": {"by": "Naomi", "text": "As for why the \"Ursprung\" was chosen, on one hand, the Ursprung is a light ST that has been battle-tested extensively. On the other hand, it probably traces back to the friendship between Dr. Harrison and Dr. Walter Newman."}}, {"title": "Testee", "text": "With years of battlefield data behind it, the Ursprung prototype's unique melee frame and \"Testee\" units had matured through clandestine upgrades. To meet the demands of the frontlines, the UNCS wove the unbound Nova-Frame into the NED series. Whether Walter Newman's rebellion was tied to this choice remains uncertain, yet Harrison's Ursprung lab pressed on relentlessly. Laniakea's trials revealed that the liberated Nova-Frame unlocked a pilot's full potential, while the re-engineered \"Testee\" units endowed the STs with unmatched agility and force across every tactical scenario."}, {"title": "The Untainted", "text": "With Laniakea's substantial investment in Ouroboros, the \"Testee\" unit was ultimately reborn as the \"Immaculateur.\" Capable of sweeping up battlefield data and recalibrating strikes in an instant, it turned every pilot into a close-combat predators. Coupled with a massive engine, the machines now moved and struck with power no one had foreseen.", "comment": {"by": "Anonymous User", "text": "It's just some superficial rhetoric... Collecting information on terrain and enemy units within range and then adjusting posture... Hahaha, is this antique technology, which was already implemented on old Type II models, really something worth boasting about? If this is the best Laniakea and the UNCS can do, then they're nothing but cowards hiding behind empty words."}}, {"title": "Bleak Future", "text": "\"...I'm sorry, Walter. In the end, our final result was taken by those people. I had little choice... You may blame me, but I never had your courage—the courage to resist them to the bitter end, even if it meant burning every bridge. I feared that my family, like yours, would fall under the UNCS's threats. In the end, I was weak. As for Aynis, she has chosen the very path you once tried so hard to keep her from. At times I even feel it was never a matter of choice at all, but destiny. You chose your road, she chose hers... and I have chosen mine. Now, this 'Immaculateur' has completed its final test, and it is about to be installed into the 'Ursprung' frame, becoming the joint masterpiece of Laniakea and the UNCS. Before long, it will be sent to Milkhama, to bear witness to the struggles of this generation. I am old now, Walter. When I look back on a life bound by chains, I wonder if I ever truly lived it. But by the time I ask myself these questions, the chance to choose has already slipped away. All that remains is my blessing, and the hope that those who come after us may find a future more merciful than ours.\"", "comment": {"by": "Researcher", "text": "Harrison often recalled with fondness his student years, and above all the afternoon when Dr. Walter Newman burst into his lab clutching the Nova-Frame report. But he often lamented that the decision to continue the research that afternoon was his biggest regret in life... I always thought that only people like me struggled with contradictions like that—but it turns out that even the doctors do too."}}]}, "20900103": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "Obsidian"}], "introduction": "NV-XX90 Pascal\nThis medium ST model, born from the Obsidian and Nvidia collaboration, showcases their expertise. The striking device combines Nvidia's sleek design and strong performance with custom modifications for Milkhama's environment. Nvidia's focus on innovation will continue to boost its reputation as it explores new technological advancements.", "stories": [{"title": "Pascal's Birth", "text": "Behold the NV-XX90 Pascal, a medium ST born from the combined genius of Obsidian and Nvidia. Obsidian's mastery in crafting its structure and appearance is matched only by Nvidia's expertise in developing the latest onboard chips and electronic components. At the heart of Pascal lies Nvidia's state-of-the-art tensor computing core, seamlessly integrated into the ST's system to deliver unparalleled efficiency and adaptability. Not to be outdone, the Pascal's blaster weapon showcases the manufacturer's remarkable vision, boasting a unique thrust engine versatile enough for both competitive ST battles and diverse civilian applications."}, {"title": "Pascal's Discovery", "text": "Pascal's debut in the public eye began with a rescue operation in a dangerous situation. Its original purpose was to participate in a new concept ST exhibition held in Milthus. However, Pascal was lost during transportation and intercepted by an unknown mercenary team. To reclaim this experimental ST with world-shaking significance, Nvidia even contacted the GSA for help."}, {"title": "Pascal's Rescue", "text": "The GSA received a distress call from the manufacturer and swiftly located Pascal in a desert base northwest of Milthus. The Electric Eel Mercenary Team had captured it. The rescue mission faced challenges due to Pascal's design and the hazardous environment, but the rescue team managed to defeat the mercenaries, reprogram Pascal's identification code, and regain control."}, {"title": "Pascal's Future", "text": "Now, Pascal has finally returned to the exhibition hall in Milthus, where it is admired by researchers and ST enthusiasts from all over the world. Its story has also relieved pilots and developers concerned about its actual combat performance. It is believed that the first cross-border ST launched by Nvidia will soon be geared for actual combat on Milkhama, where its superiority through force and rapid mobility can be fully leveraged."}]}, "30370103": {"profile": [], "introduction": "ASX-666 恶兆\n安赫特公司独自研发的重型机兵，专精于远距精准射击，是晨星同盟第四世代机兵技术验证项目的重要一环。\n鉴于晨星同盟的大力支持，安赫特不计成本地为ASX-666配备了XF4C重锻框架、夹层式复合装甲和E-S全天候主动探测系统等大量尖端技术产物，确保其拥有优越的基础性能；此外还于机体全身设置了24组全波段传感器与火控辅助单元，通过整合了帕姆斯系统的「寂灭驱动」统筹完成自动化监测、判断和锁定，大幅提升远距精准射击能力的同时有效减轻了机师的操作负担，提升了参与体系作战时的作战效能。尽管性能表现如此优秀，但晨星同盟却始终没有将该机正式列装部队，据说这与其开发、测试以及转移过程中发生的一系列事故有所关联。"}, "10340103": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "SEED"}], "introduction": "SAT-47SC Prometheus\nA third-generation Light ST spearheaded by SEED, fielded primarily by the Dawnstar League Armored Forces and the Oversight Committee.\nAs SEED's flagship model in the high-end Light ST sector, the Prometheus abandons the company's traditional focus on firepower and cost-effectiveness. It utilizes a new arashium alloy frame that is lighter and stronger, along with an experimental combat auxiliary system, the \"Delphi System,\" and features AI dynamic function control design. This allows it to efficiently gather battlefield data and deliver precise firepower with low overall energy consumption, effectively targeting high-value targets. Both technical specifications and combat results demonstrate that the Prometheus is an excellent ST for extended solo special operations missions.", "stories": [{"title": "Tech Expansion", "text": "As a long-established defense manufacturer, SEED has long held a dominant share of the DL arms market through its large-scale production and strong cost performance. However, its main competitor, Horizon, has grown rapidly in recent years, steadily eroding SEED's market share with new ST models, including the high-end light unit Rex, which has gained favor with the DLAF. At the same time, companies like An-Holt, Obsidian, and even Laniakea have been expanding into the light ST segment, further intensifying competition and raising concerns within SEED's board.\nIn December, XC 112, SEED officially launched the development of its third-generation light ST, codenamed SAT-47."}, {"title": "New Frame", "text": "Thanks to its experience in medium and heavy ST design, along with strong modular manufacturing capabilities, SEED encountered few obstacles in the SAT-47 program. In fact, development progressed faster than expected. The overall design was finalized in August, XC 113, prototype frameworks were completed by May, XC 114, assembly and structural testing followed in July, and by the end of XC 114, all early-stage validation work had been completed.\nHowever, developing a high-end ST is never without challenges. During prototype construction, SEED found that its standard Arashium Alloy offered sufficient strength but was too heavy. Using it for the SAT-47 frame would force a trade-off between mobility and payload, undermining its ability to compete with Rex. Fortunately, the Defense Forces' Advanced Weapons Research Institute already had a potential solution."}, {"title": "Brand New System", "text": "In exchange for transferring two prototype units, SEED secured a new Arashium Alloy frame from the Defense Forces' Advanced Weapons Research Institute. This new frame combined high strength with reduced weight, allowing the SAT-47 to achieve a more balanced trade-off between mobility, armor, and payload.\nWith the core engineering issue resolved, development returned to schedule. In April, XC 115, the first prototype completed structural assembly and entered a series of tests, including engine output, balance, payload, and fire control accuracy, delivering strong overall results. At the same time, SEED's Special Systems Division developed a new combat support system, the \"Delphi System,\" along with an AI-based dynamic control system. Its ability to prioritize and suppress disrupted enemy targets aligned well with the SAT-47's design philosophy, and it was incorporated into subsequent upgrades."}, {"title": "Special Ops Variant", "text": "After multiple rounds of testing and refinement, the latest SAT-47 prototype passed joint acceptance by SEED and the DLAF. Orders soon followed, including a notable one from the Oversight Committee, which also requested further specialized modifications. Seizing the chance to strengthen ties beyond the military, SEED's Prometheus design team adapted the platform for long-duration solo operations, upgrading the data link for better intel gathering and refining fire control parameters to improve mid- to long-range accuracy.\nThe result was the SAT-47SC, later named \"Prometheus,\" a special operations variant built on the SAT-47's strong adaptability. Reports suggest that over ten units have been deployed by the Oversight Committee, though details on operators and combat records remain undisclosed."}]}, "33010103": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "Obsidian"}], "introduction": "REV-00 Dawnbringer-00\nA Heavy ST developed by Obsidian. Its factory settings and development positioning were referenced from two other models codenamed Dawnbringer. REV-00 is a Heavy ST developed to adapt to the combat styles of REV-01 and REV-02. Its \"Ascendancy Core\" can continuously boost firepower and kinetic warheads in high-intensity battles, while its efficient external armor can effectively defend against enemy attacks, providing combat space for allies.", "stories": [{"title": "Development Phase 01", "text": "\"Although the Child has adapted to the bipedal humanoid ST's controls,we must remember this is a Heavy ST meant to face Leviathan. Without modifications to both the unit and armaments, it could easily become an impossible burden for a Child in fierce engagements... To be frank, we are not entirely confident we can produce an ST capable of supporting high-intensity combat in this time frame. Yet, considering the other manufacturers have poured their best technologies and manpower into improving the other REV STs, as the world's leading ST manufacturer, we will never concede defeat.\" — Report from Obsidian Personnel"}, {"title": "Development Phase 02", "text": "\"I must say, that child named Rei Ayanami doesn't talk very much, does she? During the Interview Record for pilots, she barely said anything beyond one-word answers and basic information. However, after watching her combat footage, we saw a different side of her, brave and determined... After careful observation, we were able to bring this information together to custom-tailor Rev-00 for her habits and combat style.\" — Report from Obsidian's development staff."}, {"title": "Development Phase 03", "text": "\"Although we have already witnessed their abilities and know the otherworldly nature of these Children, whenever they speak of the Evangelion units they once piloted, it's hard not to be curious about their operating principles, the way they fought... Fortunately, these are gifted Children, and we can tell they have experience. They understand that some aspects are difficult for us to reproduce... Still, I know that what we ultimately create will be very different from their old units. Perhaps the only real familiarity will be the paintwork...\" — Report from Obsidian Personnel"}, {"title": "Development Phase 04", "text": "\"On the day before the battle against Leviathan, REV-00 was finally completed. In the end, we had no choice but to repurpose parts from existing mechs and fine-tune them for the build—the only solution left to us. But when that Child climbed into the cockpit for the test run, she actually thanked us... a rarity indeed. I couldn't help but think back to when I was her age, worrying about school and grades, while they—kids like her—are being sent out into a life-or-death battle. It makes me hope that, one day, the wars will truly end, the Children can return home, and STs will disappear forever.\" — Report from Obsidian Personnel"}]}, "23010103": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "Horizon"}], "introduction": "REV-01 Dawnbringer-01\nA Medium ST developed jointly by the DL and Horizon, based on an experimental model developed by Peter Ludwig. The REV-01 is equipped with Horizon's latest arashium alloy frame and a customized OS for special pilots. The REV-01 abandons the deployment interface and space for shoulder-based tactical weapons, replacing it with an arashi particle storage device. When the arms are damaged, it can instantly repair them using stored arashi particles, significantly increasing the ST's combat efficiency and adaptability on the battlefield.", "stories": [{"title": "Log Record A", "text": "\"I'm tired of being compared to Lucas, tired of failing over and over, only to be mocked by those who don't understand anything! I've endured enough. I've worked hard enough... carried enough! Just because of that person, I'm unworthy of respect? Just because he created something better, must my work be dismissed!? As the person in charge, the leader... they just don't understand the burden I've carried, the sacrifices I've made... If I didn't have to bear these, I'd easily surpass him. And if he were to do my job, he would be nothing... Nothing! Just wait, I'll show all of you... with this unprecedented bipedal ST, with all my heart and effort... I will prove it to you!\" — Ludwig's Private Journal"}, {"title": "Log Record B", "text": "\"Fate always surprises... Lucas is dead, and those who laughed at me and dismissed me have suddenly seemed to vanish. It's as though once he was gone and the comparison between us ceased to exist, a part of me ceased to exist... But it doesn't matter, I never had any expectations for these people anyway... Whether this ST succeeds or not, as long as I can continue my research, as long as it gives me a way to survive—I'll keep on going. Perhaps I can even prove that even without Lucas, without all the resources of so-called key projects, I can still create something truly great, and prove that I am a ST researcher worthy of respect...\" — Ludwig's Intrusion Log"}, {"title": "Log Record C", "text": "\"To my surprise, the progress of REV-01 is much smoother than I imagined, yet the results were dismissed by the military evaluators. The ST's skill threshold is too high, they argue, making mass production unfeasible. I told them my research is meant to push the boundaries of Arashi Material, not merely to create weapons for profit... They were not convinced. The rest of the institute is on edge, fearing the collapse of the project... But their fears are pointless—Heinz will take care of those evaluators, and silence the shortsighted politicians who scorn this scientific legacy. I suppose this is the quiet understanding unique to accomplices.\" — Ludwig's private journal"}, {"title": "Interview Record X", "text": "\"I must say, even I am taken aback by this work. It's a masterpiece. Perhaps Professor Ludwig... well, we should no longer refer to him as \"professor\"... this criminal appears to have truly grasped the essence of the Arashi Particle, surpassing even the work of Leviathan. For such a work of genius, sacrificing the shoulder-weapon mount is a mere side note. Especially since it was crafted for that boy Shinji Ikari, such \"defects\" are completely irrelevant... Still, the sad thing about Ludwig is—and to be clear, I am not excusing that criminal—he spent his entire life seeking recognition, but he was blind to the respect he had already earned. Despite being a genius, he viewed himself as a mediocrity... It's a cruel irony.\" —Interview Record of Horizon Company's Researcher"}]}, "13010103": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "Laniakea"}], "introduction": "REV-02\nA Light ST jointly developed by the UNCS and Laniakea. Originally developed as a test machine for the next generation of Light Arashium STs, it underwent significant changes during development and became a specially crafted ST for a specific pilot. To accommodate the pilot's fighting style, REV-02 adopts a design approach completely different from regular single-core STs. REV-02 uses a highly compatible polymorphic adaptive framework in the body and legs, allowing the OS for different modules to be temporarily programmed according to the pilot's own style, ensuring compatibility while significantly increasing the efficiency of ST module usage.", "stories": [{"title": "New Type Test Machine", "text": "With the popularization of the \"Dedicated Mech\" concept, major manufacturers and various forces have entered the fray, initiating a new generation of ST R&D targeting hypothetical pilot models. Laniakea, closely cooperating with the UNCS government, has also secretly intervened in the \"Hyper-Aptamer Project\" led by Blair Bluecher. REV-02 was included in Laniakea's R&D plan as the first batch of dedicated mechs for Hyper-Aptamer pilots, and the first prototype of this production line was completed in XC 114.", "comment": {"by": "Natalia", "text": "Actually, the text here contains some inconsistencies regarding the serial numbers... After all, the three REV units come from completely different manufacturers and researchers, each with their own numbering systems... But, out of respect for the pilots' wishes, let's classify their mechs as the same series."}}, {"title": "Ill-Fated Experiment", "text": "However, the situation on Milkhama Island has changed dramatically. Due to Blair's downfall and the loss of research personnel, the Hyper-Aptamer Project on Milkhama Island has been forced to pause, and the specially developed STs for Hyper-Aptamer pilots have also been impacted. Although the new NDF authorities still intend to retain the old technological Legacy, they continue to train pilots to adapt to new STs. However, there are still not enough suitable candidates to adapt to these special STs developed for super pilots. With the failure of the research, the development line of Hyper-Aptamer STs has also been forced to pause, and REV-02, like other Experimental STs, has fallen into a long slumber in the UNCS warehouse."}, {"title": "Fated Girl", "text": "The REV-02 was undeniably lucky. Deep in the darkness of the Underground Base, it waited for its destined pilot—a red-haired girl from another world, Asuka Shikinami Langley. Built with arashium alloy technology, it was very different from the EVA unit Asuka knew, but no obstacle was too big for her brilliance. With guidance from Ophelia and the GSA, the REV-02 received significant upgrades in performance, armor, OS, and weapon compatibility, with numerous adjustments and optimizations made to suit Asuka's piloting style. Through the combined efforts of the UNCS and Laniakea, this once-abandoned Light ST was reborn in bright red. Together with Asuka, it was ready to face whatever the future would bring.", "comment": {"by": "Ophelia", "text": "Give credit where it's due. That was her victory. I'm not the kind of person to whine about losing."}}, {"title": "Perfect Answer", "text": "\"Before that girl arrived, no pilot had ever made an ST perform actions like throwing, leaps or flips. They seemed to have no tactical significance. This is because it requires the ST to be light, flexible and powerful enough, while also demanding an exceptionally strict sync ratio between the ST and the pilot. However, after observing this girl's piloting habits, we decided to try it on the REV-02. And, well, this otherworldly girl is... remarkable. She not only quickly adapted to the Dive device installed on the ST but also completed those incredible maneuvers without modifying the OS... It seems that Agent Ophelia's insistence on her abilities may not have been unfounded. Betting the REV-02, or even the entire ST production line on her, might really be worth a try.\" — Report submitted by Laniakea ST researcher."}]}, "30320103": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "Katana"}], "introduction": "RT-102A Ranger\nThis innovative heavy ST, a collaboration between Katana and Obsidian, represents their second release in the Arashium Frame series.\nWith an advanced arashium transmission core and Obsidian technology, it provides pilots seamless access to its neural system for superior control. Its high operational demands restrict usage to a select few, sparking discussions about its elite user base.", "stories": [{"title": "Special Edition", "text": "Ranger is Katana's second business model, designed for unspecified purposes and target users. According to publicly released information, Ranger's High-Load Dive Frame allows qualified pilots to achieve a super-high synchronization rate beyond the technological threshold, ensuring absolute control over heavy firepower weapons."}, {"title": "Qualified Subject", "text": "In the experiments with Aynur, certain individuals showed promise but couldn't match the Ranger's performance. After over thirty minutes in an overloaded state, most test subjects suffered mental health issues. Five individuals were lost, and further adaptations to Ranger were suspended, with only Aynur remaining as a test pilot. Report SI-2973 details Aynur Derya's specialized human modifications, which have reduced her emotional capacity but that allow her to handle the immense data flow from the Dive connection to the Ranger.", "comment": {"by": "Cicero", "text": "Apart from direct brain surgery modifications, the Predators' lab has developed a series of drugs—MM42, EM14, and KM23—to suppress memory and neural reflexes. Curiously, this Ranger's cockpit lacks a drug injection device. Is this an intentional omission?"}}, {"title": "The Other Side of the Sea", "text": "The Ranger's full potential has been realized through Aynur Derya's ability to use its full combat power, unlike the NDF elite pilots, who can only exert 50%. This has informed the development of subsequent models, using heavy STs for melee combat and light STs for reconnaissance. However, some essential-level military officers have opposed this decision due to the lack of training documentation for the Ranger's piloting method. As a result, the production and development of the Ranger may soon be stalled due to pilot selection challenges.", "comment": {"by": "Cicero", "text": "Most DLAF pilots are still unaware of the concept of the Hyper-Aptamer, but given the UNCS's tendency to stir things up, it's only a matter of time before it becomes public knowledge."}}, {"title": "Missing Reference", "text": "Although Obsidian revealed a skilled pilot could control the Ranger well, Skynet quickly suppressed the news. Despite ongoing debates surrounding suitable pilots for the Ranger, many have lost interest due to its challenging handling. Nonetheless, Katana remains motivated to improve the Ranger, buoyed by fresh investment from Obsidian, and plans to develop a new model with a high driving threshold.", "comment": {"by": "Naomi", "text": "Some sources indicate that Katana, an ST manufacturer based in the Far East, is controlled by a high-ranking member of the Obsidian group. Katana's ST development pipeline is essentially designed to test extreme research and development plans prohibited or not approved by Obsidian headquarters."}}]}, "20560103": {"profile": [], "introduction": "LTX-AB01 君权\n由拉尼亚凯亚公司为布吕希尔家族专门研发的中型指挥特化机兵，传闻由驾驶员亲自参与设计、调试。\nLTX-AB01在设计上彻底服务于“优势战术”的核心理念，其搭载的“法典”战术决策系统，是拉尼亚凯亚在信息战领域的尖端结晶。该系统能通过机体各部的广域传感器阵列，实时采集并融合战场上的光学、电磁、声纹等一切信息，在布吕希尔家族提供的海量作战数据支持下，通过解构敌方的阵型动态、弹药消耗、通讯模式甚至个体机兵的战术习惯，在驾驶员的最终调整下，能够近乎实时地推演出未来数种战场态势，精准预判敌方的薄弱环节与我方的最优行动路径。最终，系统会将唯一的“最优解”化为简洁的战术敕令呈递给驾驶员，将信息优势转化为不可逆转的胜利。"}, "10120103": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "Horizon"}], "introduction": "HR-901 Rex\nIntroducing Rex, Horizon Corporation's light model designed to compete with the Dopplesoldner and the Glasya.\nIt features a heavy weapon balancing module and advanced Arashium transmission. Equipped with the latest [M-SWIR Scope], it delivers exceptional reconnaissance and ballistic correction. Prioritizing speed over armor, it includes plating only in vital areas, relying on agility and dodging strategies for defense.", "stories": [{"title": "Fated Showdown", "text": "The competition was fierce, not only between pilots but also among STs. In August of XC 110, Doll Industries unveiled their first melee ST, the Glasya, while Obsidian introduced the Dopplesoldner, one of their top three light STs. This ignited a rivalry between the Glasya and Dopplesoldner. In September of XC 110, Horizon quietly debuted the Rex, intensifying the competition."}, {"title": "Shifting Conviction", "text": "Initially, Rex was overshadowed in the clash between Glasya and Dopplesoldner. Against the compelling narratives of these two STs, Horizon, the creator of Rex, struggled to garner attention compared to industry giants like Obsidian and the rising Doll Industries. Rex's initial launch could have been more impressive, being limited to fulfilling official orders for the DLAF, and with no plans for broader market availability.\nHowever, Rex disrupted the escalating conflict between Glasya and Dopplesoldner. Following a confrontation in XC 114, the wreckages of two mass-produced Glasya and a Dopplesoldner with the Predator emblem were discovered in the western desert. Though initially believed to have destroyed each other in combat, a closer examination revealed that neither side was responsible for the damage. Instead, it became clear that an external force had entered the scene, orchestrating the simultaneous defeat of both Glasya and Dopplesoldner.", "comment": {"by": "Grant", "text": "Why is there so much discussion about the Glasya and Dopplesoldner? According to the experts, they belong to the \"third generation STs\" that sparked a design revolution after the war."}}, {"title": "Who is the King?", "text": "Based on the evidence left at the scene and recent satellite imagery, it's highly likely that Rex, the light ST developed by Horizon, destroyed those STs. This revelation caused a sensation, drawing attention from the military, manufacturers, pilots, and ST enthusiasts. Despite denials from the DL, the media quickly seized on the news, propelling the once-overlooked Rex into the spotlight as a formidable force on the battlefield. Horizon was suddenly lauded as a premier ST manufacturer, and orders for the Rex flooded in.", "comment": {"by": "Naomi", "text": "The DL had documented the Rex strike, a necessary measure to eliminate a threat. However, widespread public speculation had already reached the point of entrenched conspiracy theories. Despite the unequivocal official statements made by the DL authorities, they struggled to contain the dissemination of these fantastical rumors."}}, {"title": "Aftermath of a Debate", "text": "The debate over the king of the new ST generation continues among enthusiasts. Extensive research has revealed the distinct advantages of the Dopplesoldner, Glasya, and Rex, each excelling in close combat, assault, and sniping, respectively.\nThis explicit specialization fuels ongoing discussions, making it a popular and enduring topic.", "comment": {"by": "Pip", "text": "That's ridiculous! The Dopplesoldner is the apex of light ST design! Whether it's melee, assault, or ranged ability, Dopplesoldner always comes out on top! If you've got something to say, stop spamming it all over Skynet and challenge us offline!"}}]}, "10290103": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "Obsidian"}], "introduction": "ELE-07 SEFAS\nA high-performance model specially developed by Obsidian, and initially commissioned by the Electric Eel.\nMany of this model's parts deviate from international standards, including the thickness of the drive rods, the size of the articulating bearings, and the location of the armor mounts.\nThe body of this ST is fitted with spikes and ramming nails in the knee and shoulder positions—features rarely seen on standard mechs—allowing it to effectively engage in close-quarters combat.", "stories": [{"title": "The Path of Symbiosis", "text": "SEFAS stands apart, every component tweaked from standard. Rough mods welded on, unpolished seams everywhere. Time reveals their purpose, Frida's will fused into steel."}, {"title": "The One", "text": "That shoulder horn? Pure irony. Her \"ride-or-die\" partner turned traitor during a drop, shredded SEFAS's shoulder with a pile driver. Cargo split, crew split, all eyes on Frida. Next fight, she rammed that new horn straight through his cockpit. Electric Eel's got one boss. Horn's still there, waiting for the next \"friend\" to try.", "comment": {"by": "Movme", "text": "Awesome, hook me up with one."}}, {"title": "Blazing Hot", "text": "The horn on ST's left knee stands as a testament to Frida's burning passion. Love struck unexpectedly, crystal clear and raw. She fell for the mysterious gentleman who serenaded her with violin at the banquet, resplendent in his black suit. She dreamed of their future—a private island, a yacht in tranquil tropical waters, endless days on golden beaches. Her ST now carries dozens of metal bone reinforcements, without them, her massive frame would crumble. Her knee horn crushed his ST into twisted steel, though he survived. \"One last question,\" Frida chose to release him. \"Did you love me?\" \"I did.\" He returned to his homeland, where justice, law, and arbitration reign and he was but one of their instruments."}, {"title": "Unknown", "text": "SEFAS and Frida, one being now. Each dent and weld tells a story. That love-starved girl's gone. Her path? Only she knows."}]}, "13020103": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "Donau Corporation"}], "introduction": "AWT(A) EX-EX Shadowrabbit vAGUE/Head: Shiva\nZeke Steel utilized the production line of Laniakea to develop a Light ST. Its prototype was the model \"ALTER-AWT\" that once thrived in the Complex. Known for being easy to mod and with broad compatibility, it became a favorite in the mercenary market. Leveraging these features, Zeke Steel made significant changes to the AWT. Overcoming the original frame's stability and energy conversion efficiency issues, he replicated ND technology through an arashium alloy frame. The vAGUE body was redesigned based on the BFB unit [Shadow Thunder], and according to Zeke Steel's vision, the \"Shadowrabbit\" was born. Its drive device and fire control system allow it to sport high-speed maneuverability while maintaining ranged precision. It's able to relentlessly engage in high-intensity combat, bolting from foe to foe like a wild rabbit.", "stories": [{"title": "Shadowtroops", "text": "How can the technology of Milkhama be used to revive ND technology? How can Arashi Material be made to exhibit properties similar to ND ore? And through what means can the full potential of Arashi Material be drawn out? Ultimately, the \"ALTER-AWT,\" circulating through the arms black market, became the vessel for Zeke's wild ideas. As a generation 1.5 mech, the Advanced Walking Tank, while unlocking its performance, also presents many issues that cannot be ignored: non-standard industrial design, non-compliant skeletal structure, and unstable compatibility modules. However, today, these issues have become advantages. The \"flexible blanks\" of the original design significantly reduced the technological gap between the two worlds. With the help of Laniakea's customized design, Zeke finally overcame these technical challenges, allowing this blueprint mech to really hold its own on Milkhama. But strictly speaking, Zeke Steel did not approach the development of the mech with a designer's mindset; rather, he treated the development itself as a scientific experiment—starting everything from scratch, would there be any difference?"}, {"title": "Selection", "text": "The landing of the Shadowrabbit was merely the beginning for Zeke. As the developer of the first-ever AWT, he knew that the only way to really understand something is to push it to its limits. The development of the Shadowrabbit was akin to re-examining the development logic of AWTs, as if starting from the drawing board. He aimed to fully exploit the development of Laniakea material on this ST. Modification, testing, destruction, splicing... The production line's load did not decrease with the landing of the ST; instead, it rose to a new level. On this unique AWT, you can see the body design of Laniakea, the drive module of Doll Industries, the fire control system of Horizon, and even the prefabricated parts of Obsidian. The design philosophy of this ST is as obsessive as Zeke Steel himself. He added every part he could access without hesitation, all to reach the so-called \"limit.\""}, {"title": "Arashi's Choice", "text": "Even the generous collaborator never expected that the concept contained in Zeke's words could become a reality. Disparate components from various arms manufacturers were coupled together like building blocks under the influence of Arashi Particles, forming an extreme and exquisite dynamic balance, ultimately constructing this Shadowrabbit. As for whether this is a miracle or a coincidence pieced together by madness, perhaps no one knows except Zeke himself. The creation that touches the \"limit\" also possesses the power of the \"limit.\" The advanced technologies from multiple arms factories are fully embodied in this machine, making the Shadowrabbit comparable to those prototypes in the lab, whether in combat performance or machine construction. Ironically, the AWT framework initially used as the foundation has instead become the limiter that the Shadowrabbit cannot surpass. Perhaps for Zeke, no matter how many times he starts over, he seems destined to tread a similar path, but the Shadowrabbit should not stop here."}, {"title": "Entrusted to Chance", "text": "\"Dr. Lando, haven't I told you? This Shadowrabbit is a byproduct of the Arashi Matter Application Experiment, our precious and only research sample. All subsequent handling and arrangements must follow my instructions... Heh, you know very well, don't you? The people of the Revival Front are not worthy of this ST. Those fools who talk about righteousness can do nothing with it but fight and kill—they can't create any other value. This Shadowrabbit will have a more suitable destination. Oh? You ask why it's named 'Shadowrabbit'? Well, that's an interesting question... What we explore always leads to uncertain results. Do you know the hares on the prairie? These creatures are keen and swift, shadows that flash before the eyes of hunters. The male hare's legs are vigorous, the female hare's eyes are blurred, and the two hares run side by side... Before catching up with the hare, how can one tell if it's male or female? The only constant is the lively, bouncing hare.\""}]}, "13030103": {"profile": [], "introduction": "DMS-001 影虎\n由西塞罗博士设计，多尔工业制造的轻型机兵。该机拥有高纯度岚质框架与新式复合装甲，兼具优秀的攻防性能。此外，精细调整过的传感辅助系统也使得它在中近距离作战中拥有无与伦比的突破能力。"}, "20550103": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "Horizon"}], "introduction": "HR-300X Snowyowl\nA Medium repair and support ST developed under the leadership of Horizon, currently deployed in limited numbers for combat testing and data collection.\nTo effectively support high-intensity ST operations and align its product line with contemporary combat systems, Horizon established the development plan for the HR-300X multifunctional support ST, culminating in the prototype codenamed \"Snowyowl.\" For this model, Horizon shifted focus from precision and burst firepower to armor load, maneuverability, and tactical data links, equipping it with fifteen sets of algorithm accessories for real-time optimal configuration. This series of designs endows the unit with exceptional continuous combat capabilities, while also enabling real-time battlefield monitoring to provide efficient repair and support to multiple ally tactical units.", "stories": [{"title": "New Demands", "text": "\"Horizon units are devastating on the battlefield, but once damaged, their precision-built, non-standard parts become a logistics nightmare.\"\nIn Horizon's original vision, these high-end, precision-crafted units were meant for highly efficient asymmetric warfare, and the performance of models like Rex proved that approach was sound. However, the pace of change exceeded expectations. Modern armored doctrines evolved rapidly, new competitors kept emerging, and the situation on Milkhama grew increasingly chaotic. The battlefield had become far more complex than anticipated. As Horizon's high-end units began losing effectiveness under varied conditions and could not be repaired in time, the company realized it needed a new platform—one that could sustain operations in complex environments while supporting and integrating with team-based combat. Around the same time, their largest backer, the DLAF, raised the same requirement, leading to the launch of the HR-300X multi-role support mech program."}, {"title": "Temporary Improvement", "text": "Although Horizon entered the high-end support mech field relatively late, its collaboration with the DLAF provided valuable data and testing opportunities. This greatly accelerated development, and within two months, the team proposed over twenty design concepts.\nAfter evaluating combat performance, cost, and future potential for bionic framework upgrades, Horizon selected Proposal 19 and quickly moved into production and testing. To meet stability and sustainability requirements, the HR-300X drew on prior designs, simplifying and restructuring modules from units like Rex and Alicorn. By sacrificing non-critical metrics, the platform achieved high compatibility across Horizon's advanced units. The process was complex, but overall progress remained steady.\nHowever, the DLAF soon introduced new requirements. They wanted the HR-300X to provide effective field repair and support for most deployed units, not just Horizon models, without significantly increasing cost. This unexpected demand brought development of the full prototype to a prolonged halt."}, {"title": "Unexpected Inspiration", "text": "With the DLAF test deadline approaching, a key module of the HR-300X still faced integration issues. Just as Horizon's team considered delaying delivery, a breakthrough in Arashi-based neural systems from the mainland provided a new solution. The full prototype was completed and successfully brought online just three days before testing.\nAfter a week of complex trials, the HR-300X met 98% of all requirements, with core metrics in field repair and area support exceeding expectations. While some refinements remained, its overall performance was enough to satisfy the DLAF. The updated prototype and its production variants were soon delivered for extended testing, and the platform received its official designation: \"Snowyowl.\"", "comment": {"by": "Elise", "text": "I've also been keeping an eye on that Arashi neural systems research. The idea of using artificial neural structures to build flexible, non-traditional wiring is impressive, and the differential evolution approach is pretty clever too. If I ever get the chance, I'd like to talk it over with the person behind it."}}, {"title": "Snowyowl's First Call", "text": "Routine performance testing of Snowyowl within the DLAF has largely been completed, but with the looming risk of a Milkhama war, the platform must prove it can be rapidly deployed at scale. This depends not only on production capacity, but also on how well it integrates with existing combat systems. To verify this, the Defense Forces advanced field trials, assigning prototypes to different units for live missions, ensuring it meets the \"three-wide\" principle—effective across multiple platforms, environments, and combat scenarios.\nInterestingly, while all deployed Snowyowl units showed strong system compatibility, their battlefield roles diverged significantly—mobile repair hubs, command relays for autonomous units, and forward support platforms for assault teams. Even Professor Kator, lead designer of the HR-300X, noted that Snowyowl's versatility exceeded expectations, offering valuable insights for Horizon's future mech development."}]}, "10400103": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "Doll Industries"}], "introduction": "DD-720 Tengshe\nA Light ST developed in collaboration with the Doll Group.\nThe Tengshe features a radical innovations in exterior design and armor material selection, significantly reducing the weight of the body while ensuring standard levels of protection. Its regular power system, along with the optimized energy-efficient \"Flame Core,\" allows the Tengshe to maintain high-speed maneuverability while loading larger and heavier weapons of mass destruction. Overall, the birth of the Tengshe has completely overturned the battlefield role of traditional Light STs.", "stories": [{"title": "Brand New Collaboration", "text": "The collaboration between the Doll Group and a certain mysterious Eastern country has a long history. Since the launch of the DD-360 Dragonrider, the Doll Group has been dashing down the path of stylization and customization. The cooperative R&D manufacturers affiliated with the Eastern country have also piqued the curiosity of the mainstream ST market and ST enthusiasts. Especially after rumors of a successor model to the DD-360 began to circulate, the market response was enthusiastic. When the concept design of the DD-720 was released, everyone was astonished that the successor to the Dragonrider was actually a Light ST. Doll Industries had seemingly abandoned its upper hand in the close-combat ST field to transition into developing heavy firepower STs. With the exposure of the cooperative R&D team, many ST enthusiasts are also curious about this new ST named Tengshe and the true nature of its development team."}, {"title": "Type Revolution", "text": "DD-720-Tengshe continues the design philosophy of Doll Industries, achieving major breakthroughs in both appearance and mech performance. Advanced alloy technology combined with a distinctive external armor structure allows Tengshe to retain effective protection while significantly reducing overall weight. At the same time, a new-generation propulsion system grants light mechs greater mobility, while also markedly increasing output capacity and weapon tolerance. As a result, Tengshe no longer fits the traditional role of light mechs as mere maneuver units for penetration tactics or battlefield reconnaissance. Instead, it gains the ability to field high-destructive weaponry, functioning as a highly mobile firepower anchor capable of dominating the battlefield."}, {"title": "Closed Roads", "text": "As many frontline engineers have noted, the current ST market has entered an era of diversification. Legacy ST manufacturers still command vast market share, yet often lack foresight and innovation when it comes to developing and transitioning to next-generation designs. In contrast, emerging ST manufacturers, seeking to break into the market, tend to concentrate resources on bold, unconventional concept STs. Units like Tengshe—STs that deliberately break traditional role definitions—are becoming increasingly common, with performance growing ever more specialized and comprehensive. It is foreseeable that as the market expands and ST technology advances, traditional ST classifications will continue to diversify. At the same time, arashium ST software design will gradually move away from unified protocol standards, shifting toward more specialized and closed architectures.", "comment": {"by": "Naomi", "text": "The apparent diversity in ST R&D is just a facade. What truly leads to the prosperity of the ST market is the confrontation and expansion of the two superpowers. The surge in order volume has flooded substantial funds into military bigwigs and the ST market. Meanwhile, the competition in armed forces provides a showcase for new weapons and new ST models."}}, {"title": "Harpy Intel", "text": "The release of Tengshe sent clear shockwaves through the ST market. Although DD-720 is still far from mass production, Doll Industries has already secured a considerable number of pre-orders. Public attention has increasingly turned toward Doll Industries' joint development partner. However, the manufacturer based in Shenzhou remains elusive. The few circulating rumors suggest that the partnership originates with Alyson Doll, the future heir of the Doll family, and an unnamed close associate who has yet to appear publicly. Given the active role played by Harpy in promoting DD-720, it is reasonable to suspect that the ST's joint developer maintains deep connections with this powerful Milkhama-based local force."}]}, "30190103": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "Doll Industries"}], "introduction": "DD-313G Thanatos\nA heavy mech developed by Dor Heavy Industries, built specifically for special operations in extreme environments.\nThe constant-temperature pilot cabin crafted using the most cutting-edge temperature control technology allows Thanatos to easily adapt to the vast majority of extreme combat environments. Whether it's the raging inferno of a sea of flames or a surprise attack lurking beneath an ice layer, pilots driving Thanatos can maintain full focus throughout and execute combat orders with precision. Its unique \"Flameflow\" core can even precisely calculate the heat capacity of enemy mechs and the environment, providing the pilot with more accurate strike information.", "stories": [{"title": "Pole-Hsia's End", "text": "I never thought things would end this way—the company's prospects are bleak, multiple ST development lines have been cut, and several component manufacturers and research labs have gone bankrupt. Since the emergence of the miraculous material Arashium, the war of ST development hasn't let up for a second, but unfortunately, we've ended up the losers. I should start thinking about retired life. Although there are \"winners\" like Kamadar and even Obsidian willing to hire me as a technical consultant, they've only agreed to employ me alone. My assistants, students, team, and partners aren't worth a thing to them. I cannot betray them. I'll stay with my old friends—whatever comes next, we'll see it through together.", "comment": {"by": "Naomi", "text": "Dr. Ferdinand used to be the technical director of a medium ST manufacturer called \"Pole-Hsia\" in the DL. After the company went bankrupt, Ferdinand refused invitations from several industry giants and went solo with his technical team."}}, {"title": "Firefighting Order", "text": "It's been four months since we left the old Pole-Hsia workshop. We've set up a new one near the reservoir in Thorleifin and are taking orders to repair and modify civilian engineering STs. Our finances are tight, and many have left. The remaining partners are hopeful, but I need more time to afford next month's salaries. Thanks to our outstanding reputation, we have been tasked with an exciting new project by the fire department—to design a state-of-the-art firefighting ST. The upfront payment is substantial, and if we can develop a solid plan in time, it could help the workshop massively."}, {"title": "Performance Boost", "text": "The funds for Project 186 have far exceeded the fire department's budget, yet there's a continual influx of money into the accounts—it's astounding! The intentions of the people leading this project are not simple. The demand for higher heat resistance and adaptability to extreme cold has led us to shift to a constant temperature system. Currently, the functions of the experimental STs for Project 186 are deviating toward military design, and the new \"constant temperature cockpit\" and computing core that adjusts performance based on the external environment have presented us with unprecedented challenges. Nevertheless, we can't afford to consider these things now. In the pursuit of excellence, we have to go all in!"}, {"title": "Lost in the Mist", "text": "Four days after completing our prototype, the truth finally came to light. The fire department's order and our account funds were legitimate, but by the time our \"Thermite\" project was finalized, the investor had changed to the \"Doll Group,\" a key ST supplier to the military. They saw our potential and brought us into their R&D under the guise of collaboration, renaming our ST DD-313G. I have accepted their terms, though I now question if it was the right choice. We'll soon lose some autonomy to our parent company, straying from our original vision. Only time will tell if this was the right move.", "comment": {"by": "Naomi", "text": "Dr. Ferdinand joined the Doll Group in June XC 113. Since then, information regarding him and his team has become highly confidential, and even I haven't been able to learn more... However, according to rumors, Ferdinand added the letter at the end of the ST's designation to commemorate a manufacturer named \"Pole-Hsia.\""}}]}, "10170103": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "Obsidian"}], "introduction": "OS-11A Twilight Fang\nOne of Obsidian's high-performance light STs, developed based on the OS-06F Diana's combat data.\nThe Twilight Fang's built-in \"Fang\" unit can forcibly calibrate the ST's actions when the pilot's operational accuracy is insufficient, ensuring mission completion.\nThis ST was designed in two models—Model A, suitable for urban terrain, and Model B, for jungle and mountain warfare. Ultimately, Obsidian chose the more versatile Model B to be mass-produced.", "stories": [{"title": "Wandering in the Dusk", "text": "Twilight Fang is an agile ST specialized in infiltration, night ops, and versatile combat. As one of Obsidian's three premium light STs, it stands apart from the Dreadtalon and Dopplesoldner's focus on coordinated strikes and decapitation missions. The Twilight Fang excels in behind-enemy-lines operations, offering Milkhama's buyers a distinct tactical edge.", "comment": {"by": "Cicero", "text": "Specs are theory. Combat's the real test."}}, {"title": "Unknown", "text": "Twilight Fang came in City (Type A) and Jungle (Type B). Slipped through mangrove channels at night, using stealth tech and terrain against DLAF. Silent hunter in the dark.", "comment": {"by": "Winston", "text": "Perfect STs might exist, but battlefields aren't perfect. Pick the best trait, deploy where needed."}}, {"title": "Special Action", "text": "During Operation Mangrove, Twilight Fang faced heavy resistance from anti-ST turrets and hidden mines. Though challenged, they proved their combat versatility. A 75mm armor-piercing round at 65x caliber only damaged one unit's outer armor, leaving its alloy frame intact. The engagement ended with two Twilight Fangs immobilized by counter-fire.", "comment": {"by": "Movme", "text": "Give us gear, we'll match any army."}}, {"title": "Type Selection", "text": "With Milkhama's sparse population density, Type B became the production model. Urban warfare falls to heavily-armed armor squads - most pilots agree deploying such advanced STs in risky street combat is wasteful. If given choice, infantry and ground armor are better suited for these operations."}]}, "20140103": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "Obsidian"}], "introduction": "OS-77 Wolverine\nA medium tactical ST with impressive firepower support capabilities, developed by Obsidian.\nThis ST is equipped with a high-power radar search and locking system and a cluster energizer to assist in the tracking and timing of projectiles, effectively improving the killing efficiency of its ordinance. Its fully optimized frame structure also ensures a certain degree of mobility, making it capable of working with high-speed armored units in combat.\nDespite its high cost, the Wolverine is desirable due to its excellent performance.", "stories": [{"title": "New Platform", "text": "The Wolverine, Obsidian's latest mecha, roars to life for the UNCS. This fire-breathing ST is built to sync with Union's lightning-fast armor squads.\nThe DLAF's devastating long-range barrage in the Milkhama War left the Union stunned and scarred. While war evolves, the hunger for firepower burns eternal. Now, we've given those big guns legs and unleashed a mobile inferno.", "comment": {"by": "Naomi", "text": "Everyone thinks mobile missile platforms are simple. \"Just mount and roll\"—if only."}}, {"title": "Second Orders", "text": "Post-war peace demands and Obsidian's pressure forced Milthus to slash city defenses. Military brass warned: removing too many missile systems from Milthus Bridge and Delta zone could leave a gaping hole in mid to long-range defense. The City Guard's solution? Acquire a handful of Wolverine mechs. These high-performance support units could plug the defense gap and keep Milthus secure."}, {"title": "Perfect Timing", "text": "In the same year as the second Wolverine batch delivery, a major scandal rocked the Milthus City Guard. Thirty ST officers were caught in an embezzlement scheme involving corruption, bribes, and falsified expense reports. The investigation uncovered massive financial fraud that crippled Milthus' defense infrastructure. Outraged citizens flooded the streets, demanding justice and severe punishment for the guilty officers."}, {"title": "Popular Demand", "text": "The Wolverine mech orders got axed as protests swelled, halting military reforms. Only a handful of delivered units remain active. Despite setbacks, both UNCS and DL media applauded Milthus' crackdown on corruption. They see it as crucial for Milthus Port's security and Milkhama Island's transparent future."}]}, "20030103": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "Obsidian"}], "introduction": "Code Unknown XR\nDesigned by Winston and produced by Obsidian, only one model of this ST was made, for one specific pilot, whose identity is not stored in its records.\nBuilt with no expense spared, the XR is equipped with a device called the \"Mirror Core,\" which operates in conjunction with a hub processor in the cockpit and mirror imagers on the left and right arms to significantly enhance efficiency. The energy circulation management system in the body and legs also ensure the ST's long-term combat capability without requiring resupplies.\nAccording to unidentified sources, the XR is linked to research related to \"Super Pilots.\" More data is needed.", "stories": [{"title": "A Concept", "text": "The special ST unit XR emerged from Winston's bold vision of future warfare. As ST development grew more specialized and high-tech, gone were the days of civilian conversions and direct factory builds. Now, researchers meticulously planned each unit, integrating cutting-edge tech and rigorous pilot testing before production. Winston approached the new ST project differently, starting with the pilot. If you know your pilot and their combat style, what could be more lethal than a machine built precisely for them?", "comment": {"by": "Naomi", "text": "Winston excels in project leadership through pragmatism, sacrificing tempting plans for realistic goals."}}, {"title": "Special Audience", "text": "Mecha Alert: XR's Femme Fatale Cockpit Conundrum! Shrinking the XR's cabin for the lady pilot? Not so fast! Winston wasn't buying it, but it'd pack more combat tech without squishing components. He dropped some Ovett ST knowledge: Quick fixes might dodge bullets now, but only big-brain thinking ensures Steel Trooper supremacy long-term. The XR prototype? Not as svelte as its blueprints. It didn't crush the competition right away, but unlimited upgrades pushed the tech to the max. Now, the new XR struts its stuff as the ultimate performance beast of its time!"}, {"title": "Mirror Core", "text": "XR's Mirror Core integrates cockpit processor with dual-arm mirrors, enabling weapon sync, tactical adaptation, and extended combat endurance through advanced energy management."}, {"title": "Independent Researcher", "text": "UNCS restrictions forced Winston to Obsidian Research Institute in Milthus. Though Obsidian-branded, UNCS controls tech. First pilot: female NDF operative."}]}, "10070102": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "Katana"}], "introduction": "RT-79S Ambusher\nThis ranged model is a light ST developed by Katana and was the first commercial model released by the company.\nIt was specialized for long-range attacks and equipped with a complete set of automatic targeting devices, providing practical assistance to the armored forces of the UNCS.\nDue to Katana's ability to customize upgrades, this ST has gained a positive reputation on the market.", "stories": [{"title": "Battlefield Blade", "text": "Ambusher (RT-79S), Katana's debut ST, proves worth during Milkhama War. UNCS acquires three test units to counter supply line vulnerabilities."}, {"title": "Counterattack Line", "text": "At Kagbo Town, three experimental Ambusher STs supported UNCS armor. Five Akers fell to 26-pound guns in 15 minutes. The Ambushers switched to offensive tactics with Michel transport support."}, {"title": "Honor of the Brave", "text": "After that battle, two survived, earning pilots Goldenem Eichenlaub. Later upgrades improved the fire control system of the Ambusher.", "comment": {"by": "Grant", "text": "Friend in 307th lost an arm at Kagbo. Lucky compared to his squad."}}, {"title": "Customized Route", "text": "Katana adapts Ambusher for global markets, earning reputation through regional customization."}]}, "20200102": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "Laniakea"}], "introduction": "LTX-24 Arash\nThis Medium ST was developed by Laniakea. It is an excellent ranged model boasting high performance, and is an essential part of the UNCS's tactical forces.\nIts multi-dot assisted aiming system grants this ST high accuracy. In contrast, using advanced polymer materials in some of its armor panels reduces its weight, giving it enough mobility to cope with combat on the front lines.", "stories": [{"title": "This is Good", "text": "The ST Arash returns to the training ground under cadet Dana's command. Though gifted, she isn't top-tier like Enfield's elite students - yet she combines talent with unmatched dedication. I oversee every combat assessment, setting targets and inspecting machine conditions. Snipers must adapt to the field, but demand perfection from their ST and rifle. Despite access to superior units, Dana stays loyal to her Arash. None dare pilot her machine - and that's exactly how it should be. —Diary, Page 3", "comment": {"by": "Naomi", "text": "Here's your diary, Dana. Found it in the belongings of its late owner. Might shed some light on things."}}, {"title": "Second?", "text": "I watch Dana's sniper positions and timing from my window overlooking the training ground. Though I only know her through the ST Arash's viewfinder, my respect stems purely from her dedication and skill. She placed second in graduation trials, leaving her confused and angry. Appeals won't change the results. —Diary, Page 10", "comment": {"by": "Dana", "text": "Hmm... Training admin spotted on grounds."}}, {"title": "No, First", "text": "The top spot goes to our own. The NDF isn't the old Ovett Army, we're alpha wolves leading the pack. Dana lacks our bonds now, but every instructor at Enfield knows she's the true number one. —Diary, Page 11", "comment": {"by": "Dana", "text": "Second is second. That first place reeks of foul play!"}}, {"title": "Destiny", "text": "News of Dana's defection from NDF stings. Her pride drove her to mercenary work instead of the bright future Enfield promised. Blair owes her for that second place. Rules demand elimination, but I'll bend them legally. Her ST Arash awaits in the next GKD Squad shipment. —Diary, Page 50", "comment": {"by": "Dana", "text": "No coincidences here... Damn, if only it were that simple."}}]}, "10130102": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "Laniakea"}], "introduction": "LTX-17 Boyer\nA mass-produced assault ST developed by Laniakea.\nThe Boyer's excellent structure has made it a standout in the history of mech design, and its stable performance in actual combat has sparked competition and imitation among various factions.\nIt is rumored that the UNCS once attempted to manufacture a more advanced LTX-18 Boyer II, but the development plan was forced to be discontinued for unknown reasons.", "stories": [{"title": "Universal Giant", "text": "Boyer excels through universal parts: An-H3 targeting, Kamadar 703 transmission, Doll type-4 engine. Achieves combat efficiency through smart assembly.", "comment": {"by": "Cicero", "text": "Boyer's designer and I went head-to-head at the college finals..."}}, {"title": "Market Competition", "text": "The ST Boyer excels in mass production with low costs and high reliability. Major powers monitor its production closely, developing countermeasures to maintain battlefield dominance."}, {"title": "Industry Foundation", "text": "The ST Boyer's brilliance lies in its mass-production potential and reliability. While its blueprints are semi-public, only UNCS can produce its precision components. Production lines across NDF cities serve both domestic forces and allies. The design emerged from a bilateral college competition, earning second place. Author's name: [■■■■]", "comment": {"by": "Cicero", "text": "Boyer's gone. That Ovettian's chance died with it. His choice, not my fault."}}, {"title": "Halfway Period", "text": "\"Path of Return\"—UNCS's classified Boyer II project. Top-tier parts fused into a mech masterpiece? Pure genius! Sadly, the mastermind behind it bit the dust during a wild night out. Even ace engineers need to blow off steam, whether they're DL or UNCS. No one's immune to the siren call of a good time!", "comment": {"by": "Naomi", "text": "Cicero's hiding something. Time for another lab \"visit.\""}}]}, "30260102": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "An-Holt"}], "introduction": "ASX-117 Charon\nA heavy ST produced by An-Holt, specialized in defense and based on the ASX-114.\nThe ASX-117 combat core is equipped with additional impact-resistant components when compared to the ASX-114 used by Gamesaurs, and its armor has been replaced with more robust and complete protective plates. These upgrades in armor make Charon the most significant and heaviest model among contemporary heavy STs.", "stories": [{"title": "New Equipment", "text": "Exiting Zealred's battered cockpit, we scored a new mech ally. Meet Charon, our fresh Steel Trooper. This beast's armor stats are off the charts—nearly double the thickness! Talk about a major upgrade in the safety department. These top-tier mechs were supposed to go to the elite 2-series armor squads, but they shipped 'em straight to us grunts instead. Looks like the brass is finally showing some love for us frontline pilots. Not gonna complain about that!\n—Corporal Lars, 4/12 XC 110", "comment": {"by": "Winston", "text": "The Charon mecha units rolled off the production line in March 110 NE. They hit the frontlines in April. We need real combat data, so let's deploy these bad boys where the action's hottest!"}}, {"title": "Corporal's Perfect ST", "text": "Let's dive into Charon's specs... This bad boy's got a souped-up ST core based on the Gamesaurs ASX-114. Its turbo engine packs a serious punch, hitting a blistering 85 km/h, leaving other heavy Steel Troopers in the dust. Decked out with cutting-edge tech: composite armor, Golden Leopard rangefinder, and a slick comms system. It's a beast on paper, but the real test? Throwing it into the heat of battle. Time to see what this mech can do.\n—Corporal Lars, XC 110.4.12", "comment": {"by": "Winston", "text": "Yongchang Securities wisdom: Faith outweighs gold."}}, {"title": "Legend of Courage", "text": "Charon's our ace in the hole! This mech's so finely tuned, even our welder Little John can pilot it like a pro. For us frontliners, it's a game-changer. Rebel anti-ST guns? Useless against us. Word is, Belsuth's feeling the heat too. Assembly call's ringing - time to gear up for the next mission!\n—Corporal Lars, 4/25, XC 110", "comment": {"by": "Winston", "text": "Charon's alloy impressed me. Anti-pen's solid. Could cut tungsten and titanium, bump the nickel—make it last longer."}}, {"title": "Faith Experiment", "text": "The initial assault on the stronghold's south gate was a bust. Those crafty rebel scum dug in turrets on the cliffs, making top-down and parallel strikes useless. Now it's our turn to shine. Mission: infiltrate the canyon and obliterate those turrets up close and personal. Intel says they've got anti-armor mines and cluster bombs waiting for us. But with Charon's battlefield prowess, it's just another day at the office.\n—Corporal Lars, 4/27, XC 110"}]}, "10200102": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "Obsidian"}], "introduction": "OS-06F Diana\nA balanced light ST produced by Obsidian.\nA special interference pattern coats this ST's armor surface. The lightweight construction of its legs makes it adept at dodging.\nAs a foreign trade model, there are slight differences in the Diana's control system and engine casing for different factions.\nBased on combat data gathered by the OS-06F, Obsidian completed the development of OS-07X, OS-11A, and OS-09S.", "stories": [{"title": "Hotspot Competition", "text": "Diana's balanced design spawns Obsidian's elite trio: Dopplesoldner (OS-07X), Twilight Fang (OS-11A), Dreadtalon (OS-09S)."}, {"title": "The Gate of Eden", "text": "Year 105 Eden Core revolutionizes ST design. Exceptional compatibility enables novice pilots to match veterans. Zweihander, Dominator, and Bloodfang modules spark industry-wide core development race."}, {"title": "Technical Competition", "text": "The Diana ST is priced at 400,000 Milkhama Dollars, with a 50,000 variance based on loadout. While costly for standard forces, elite units find it worthwhile. The DL and UNCS models differ in cockpit systems and engine housing construction. DL uses one-piece SEED castings, while UNCS opts for Obsidian's sectional welded design. Despite similar strength ratings, recent DL combat data shows engine housing deformation issues, questioning SEED's local advantage. Obsidian counters with lifetime warranty coverage."}, {"title": "Trial and Improvement", "text": "During 37 battles against the Ashes, UNCS Guard deployed in 5 operations. The Diana ST engaged in 3 fights across 4 missions. Two Diana units showed reduced power after taking hits, though mobility remained intact. Post-battle inspection revealed engine weld cracks from impact damage. Obsidian implemented repairs using austenitic welding rods and stress-relief techniques.", "comment": {"by": "Grant", "text": "As an ace mech pilot, I trust the specs. But I'll put this beast through its paces to verify. Time to push the limits and see if it lives up to the hype."}}]}, "10020102": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "Laniakea"}], "introduction": "LTX-19 Flintstone\nThis melee model is a light ST developed by Laniakea. It was initially designed as a companion combat model for Arash.\nAfter several design changes, the ST adopted a new type of alloy as its skeleton material, making it both solid and lightweight and striking a good balance between maneuverability and survivability, thus becoming one of the main combat models of the NDF.", "stories": [{"title": "Pre-Design Plan", "text": "Flintstone ST originally supported Arash units but proved versatile with Chariot teams. Combat feedback led to enhanced armor, fire control, and joint systems."}, {"title": "Combat Companion", "text": "The Flintstone mech delivered crucial fire support and mobile cover for ground units, becoming a strategic linchpin for large-scale operations. But a decade of tech advancements and firepower upgrades have eroded its protective edge. Now, the ST's fragile frame and lackluster arsenal make it the Achilles' heel in tactical formations. Time for an upgrade, pilots!"}, {"title": "Flintstone Evolution", "text": "Early Flintstone models' combat flaws prompted NDF to order Laniakea improvements. Changes include fire control system space adjustments, arm transmission upgrades for enhanced firepower, and leg joint flexibility modifications. Expert analysis concludes: Add shoulder and body armor."}, {"title": "Strategic Opportunity", "text": "The Flintstone mech has evolved from a sidekick to a frontline powerhouse! Beefed-up shoulder and torso plating transformed this bot into a main battle unit. Now, Flintstone doesn't just back up the Unreachable with heavy fire. It's a game-changer on the field. With nimble moves and teamwork tactics, this mech carves out winning strategies for the whole squad.", "comment": {"by": "Grant", "text": "New Flintstone! Lab rats think light-years ahead."}}]}, "30120102": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "An-Holt"}], "introduction": "ASX-114 Gamesaurs\nA heavy ST developed and produced by An-Holt during the Milkhama War.\nEquipped with a large sliding monitor to enhance tracking and locking performance, it uses an ASX-114 combat core that allows it to specialize in combat with agile targets. Its head-mounted electronic jammer can launch electromagnetic pulses to interfere with enemy evasion systems while tracking their trajectory.", "stories": [{"title": "City Defense Configuration", "text": "As the activities of the Rebel Army in the Parill Desert region have become increasingly rampant in recent years, the UNCS has decided to place an order with An-Holt for a new ST model, which will be handed over to the White Maple Defense Army for use.\nThe new Steel Trooper, Gamesaurs, features the ASX-114 combat core and electronic jammers in its head, allowing it to track and disable enemies. However, the defense army opted not to place additional orders after field tests revealed high ammunition and logistical demands.", "comment": {"by": "Naomi", "text": "Light STs catch heat for their speed. What's wrong with being quick? Like any good hacker—get in, get out."}}, {"title": "Spikes", "text": "In XC 109, Ashes Forces unleashed lightning strikes on NDF in Parill. Rebel STs, armed with intel and superior mobility, shattered fortress defenses, severing comms between White Maple City and Sunset Valley Armored Corps. NDF casualties: 6 artillery posts, 2 radar stations, 2 ammo dumps, 1 command hub, and 1 comms relay obliterated. 3 secret hangars and 4 logistics bases faced heavy fire. NDF brass, stunned by phantom foes, scrambled to counter these hyper-mobile units. White Maple City Defense, desperate to stem the tide, demanded 25 heavy Gamesaur STs to fortify the line."}, {"title": "Urban Battle Base", "text": "After days of chaos, White Maple's defense force and allied units from Rayneburg launched a counterattack against rebels controlling the area between Sunset Valley and White Maple. The rebels' high-speed units were severely weakened by Gamesaurs, forcing a retreat. In the final phase, Gamesaurs lost sync with other mecha units, hampering the pursuit force's combat effectiveness and allowing some rebels to escape annihilation.", "comment": {"by": "Raven", "text": "The Heavy Mechs dominate local skirmishes but fall short in total annihilation. That's their Achilles' heel. To forge an unstoppable combat unit, you need a diverse arsenal of Steel Troopers working in sync. Mix and match for maximum destruction!"}}, {"title": "New Base", "text": "In XC 110, the Port Rayneburg's Gamesaurs Squad roared into action during the West Sunset Valley's endgame. These mecha-beasts bolstered the NDF's retreat from Foggy Mountain Trail, forging an impenetrable wall of steel and scales. The rebels, outgunned and outmaneuvered, had no choice but to fall back. Post-battle, Kadrey deployed these formidable Gamesaurs to fortify Saget Town's defenses.", "comment": {"by": "Naomi", "text": "NDF would rather ship Gamesaurs by rail than build more. Penny-pinchers."}}]}, "20260102": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "An-Holt"}], "introduction": "AST-06 Hermes\nAn-Holt Corporation developed this medium ST. It is mainly equipped by the tactical support forces of the Dawnstar League.\nThis model is designed to carry tactical weapons and is equipped with high-power radar, trading mobility for excellent guidance capabilities and allowing for efficient detection and the locking on of distant targets.\nAs part of the DL Tactical System, it often cooperates with the Kaolin in combat.", "stories": [{"title": "Effective Training", "text": "The Hermes: An-Holt's XC 105 fire support mech. Equipped with ultra-powerful radar, it locks onto targets 50km away using ultrasonic tech. Sales tanked due to outdated tactics, but Dawnstar snagged 5 units at 80% off. Now they're New Wright's go-to for pilot training and missile testing. A bargain beast with untapped potential!"}, {"title": "Function Expansion", "text": "Due to Hermes' specialized support firepower but limited solo combat ability, Alliance forces pair it with Gaoling units. Select Hermes models carry waterproof ST supply packs for ammo and resources. These shock-absorbing storage units ensure stable logistics for combat teams."}, {"title": "Counterflow Ambush", "text": "In NC 106, Hermes joined the Warm Current Coast defense mission. ST squads from nearby bases swiftly located Northern Union landing zones, providing crucial intel for the assault plan. Though untested and newly deployed, Hermes was chosen due to limited available forces in the coastal region.", "comment": {"by": "Marcus", "text": "Kill their radar station, blind their scouts. Some STs pack radar too. They're priority targets."}}, {"title": "As You See", "text": "The Hermes mech's pinpoint guidance and relentless barrage forced the UNCS spec ops to ditch their Lukewarm Bay beachhead in just 5 hours. The DL clinched a solid win, showcasing the superior skills of their pilots and STs. While outdated Cyclones were shredded by beach defenses, only a single Hermes fell to a heavy-caliber ST Sniper. As 106 wrapped up, An-Holt scored fresh Hermes contracts, and military academies reignited debates on high-power ST radar configs.", "comment": {"by": "Grant", "text": "This skirmish's silver lining? More missile STs in our arsenal."}}]}, "20280102": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "Laniakea"}], "introduction": "LTX-29 Ironclad\nLaniakea developed this medium assault ST mainly used by the UNCS Rapid Response Mountain Troops.\nThis model features remarkable claw-shaped feet and an automatic adjustable hydraulic transmission system. It is equipped with the \"Pursuer\" quick response buzzer on its lightweight arm, ensuring its ability to attack over complex terrain to the maximum extent. At the same time, thanks to its efficient armor structure, it still benefits from a degree of protection against medium to long-range attacks.", "stories": [{"title": "Terrain Adaptation", "text": "Laniakea's Ironclad assault ST features enhanced feet, superior grip, and auto-adjusting hydraulics for terrain stability. Reinforced body armor protects against mid-range attacks, with lightweight arms carrying pursuit quick-fire systems."}, {"title": "Hidden in the Mountains", "text": "Modified Ironclads use stealth coating to evade radar. This enabled New Wright Town infiltration, destroying Eastern Radar Station during Lukewarm Bay op. Pilots, selected from Eburgo counter-terror veterans, excel in mountain and stealth tactics.", "comment": {"by": "Marcus", "text": "Combat zones differ from counter-terror ops."}}, {"title": "Lost in the Lukewarm Bay", "text": "Ironclad suffered heavy losses at Lukewarm Bay, vulnerable to missile barrages. Despite this, mountain warfare success drives Laniakea's continued production improvements. Reports indicate new mountain ST development based on Ironclad design."}, {"title": "Rein Tactics", "text": "The UNCS pairs Wolverine with Ironclad to cover its recon and ranged combat weaknesses. Wolverine's advanced radar and ECM systems detect cloaked enemy STs and eliminate surveillance gaps, while its ranged countermeasures complement Ironclad's devastating close assault. This synergy excels in complex terrain. Despite Ironclad's limits, new UNCS pilots beam with pride at their assignment. This ST launched ace pilot Rosa's legendary career. Whether they match her glory is one thing, but sitting in that cockpit, imagining her battles, is something else entirely."}]}, "20250102": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "Horizon"}], "introduction": "HR-277 Kaolin\nHorizon Corporation developed this medium combat ST primarily deployed in the DLAF's elite troops. \nOnce a classified model of the DL, the shock-generating system built into its shoulder enhances the penetration of its armament, while the tilted armor at the front makes it a highly effective charging and counter-charging weapon, especially in the hands of skilled pilots.", "stories": [{"title": "Classified Project", "text": "The Kaolin ST's defining feature is its shoulder-mounted shock system, amplifying melee strikes with focused sonic waves. Its distinctive head design channels these waves for maximum impact. The Dawnstar League kept this devastating ST classified until Operation Lorine proved its combat effectiveness."}, {"title": "Ripples of War", "text": "Kaolin's baptism of fire at Operation Lorine yielded jaw-dropping results.\nThe UNCS came in hot, rolling deep with twin armored squads and STs. They blitzed Rayneburg Ridge, hammering the DLAF's makeshift defenses. With allies dropping like flies, Kaolin and Rex tag-teamed the assault. Radiance had their six as they stormed the Union's stronghold. Kaolin's armor-shredding prowess crushed three waves of Union forces, sending them packing.", "comment": {"by": "Gumusiay", "text": "One Kaolin? Easy prey, just keep it off the network."}}, {"title": "Technical Imitation", "text": "The UNCS salvaged a wrecked Kaolin, sending it to White Maple for a tech strip. They reverse-engineered its shoulder-mounted power core, integrating it into their own mecha. While cloning the tech was a cakewalk, mastering the high-impact shockwave system was another story. Only the most skilled pilots could harness its raw power, leaving rookies in the dust."}, {"title": "Tactical Evolution", "text": "The NDF is cooking up killer ST tactics to take down Kaolin! They're beefing up their Union STs with long-range firepower and e-warfare to cripple Kaolin before it gets up close and personal. It's all about zapping 'em from afar or blasting 'em to bits!\nAs the conflict heats up, the battlefield's become a high-tech showdown. Big guns and e-gadgets are everywhere! Some thought close-combat STs were going extinct, but hold up! The rise of those badass \"Hyper-Aptamers\" is changing the game. Now, a top-notch pilot can turn the tide of battle with sheer skill. The mech maestros are back in business!", "comment": {"by": "Rosa", "text": "From myths of warring gods to tech-driven combat, the future unfolds."}}]}, "20150102": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "Laniakea"}], "introduction": "LTX-26 Krieger\nLaniakea led the development of this Medium ST, known for its cost-effectiveness and stability. It is frequently deployed by the NDF.\nThis model utilizes a planar square structure and laser and electron beam composite welding technology to improve strength while reducing hardware failure rates and deployment time. It comes with a multi-language operating system, which has been well received by members of the NDF.", "stories": [{"title": "Embracing Diversity", "text": "The Krieger ST boasts over 650 units in NDF service. West Milkhama's population grew by 180,000 in three years. 72% from Union states, 21% from non-Dawnstar regions. While basic STs feature 3-4 language options, the Krieger ships with 15 OS languages, ensuring swift deployment of diverse pilots under NDF command.", "comment": {"by": "Arnold", "text": "Laniakea's global strategy: Production overseas, assembly in Milkhama, R&D in UNCS labs. Sets industry standard."}}, {"title": "Closed-Loop Production", "text": "The Krieger's globalization extends beyond its multilingual support to its manufacturing. Anticipating future conflicts in Milkhama and ST shortages, Laniakea outsources production to Kamadar Corp's low-cost facilities. Parts ship via international routes to Milkhama for final assembly at Laniakea's plants."}, {"title": "Quantity Advantage", "text": "Forged from southern iron, the Krieger ST emerges from Kamadar's furnace. Its flat, squared frame and top-notch welding make it a reliable warhorse. Easy fixes and scrap recycling keep these mechs in the fight. While not matching elite STs, the Krieger's strength lies in numbers, swarming battlefields en masse.", "comment": {"by": "Winston", "text": "Basic skills work, no real wars lately."}}, {"title": "Battlefield Configuration", "text": "The Krieger proves cost-effective with its multi-terrain capabilities and reliable performance in mountains, swamps, and urban zones. Anti-air vehicles supplement the ST's defense against aerial threats. This comprehensive battlefield setup allows for less stringent pilot requirements.", "comment": {"by": "Naomi", "text": "Borrowed that ST once. Multi-language system's loaded, but thank the stars for universal language mode."}}]}, "30030102": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "SEED"}], "introduction": "SAT-309 Mandrill\nA heavy melee ST developed and produced by SEED after the Milkhama War.\nThe body and shoulders of this ST are equipped with a hydraulic system made of Arashium alloy. This system automatically adjusts the pressure and flow of hydraulic systems, using gyroscopic sensors and data from targeting systems to achieve optimal thrust and torque output.", "stories": [{"title": "Hydraulic Self-Regulation", "text": "The SAT-309 \"Mandrill\" is a cutting-edge Melee ST that showcases the Dawnstar League's mastery of Arashium tech. This mecha beast sports state-of-the-art Arashium Alloy hydraulics on its shoulders, torso, and weapon mounts. The system auto-adjusts pressure and flow based on pilot input and target dynamics, maximizing thrust and torque output.\nSEED Manufacturing beefed up the Mandrill's close-quarters prowess by reinforcing its shoulders and arms. They also bulked up its frame and hardened its armor, making this war machine a true monster in melee combat."}, {"title": "Pre-War Deployment", "text": "The Mandrill: A powerhouse mech with devastating offense and unmatched durability. Engineered to counter UNCS heavy artillery on the Foren River, it's built to survive and demolish riverine defenses. After the Foren River clash, SEED Manufacturing scored big R&D bucks. The DLAF swiftly snatched up these beasts, arming their elite armored battalions with unstoppable firepower.", "comment": {"by": "Winston", "text": "Ceramic armor works on tanks. ST shell complexity blocks wider use, but custom fits are doable."}}, {"title": "Constant Propulsion", "text": "When the Lorine Conflict erupted, the DLAF banked on Mandrill's frontline prowess, deploying it as the spearhead in multiple siege assaults. Each operation typically unleashed 10+ Mandrills alongside 15+ Hermes units, pushing for over 3 grueling hours. Yet, Mandrill's battlefield performance fell short of expectations. Despite its impenetrable armor shrugging off most artillery fire, relentless barrages significantly slowed its advance. This caused ST formations to lose cohesion, ultimately stalling the offensive. The Mandrill's combat effectiveness proved less than stellar in the year's intense theatre of war.", "comment": {"by": "Grant", "text": "Can't kill Mandrills, but pinning them works just fine."}}, {"title": "Beyond War", "text": "In July, the DLAF 305th Armored Battalion faced an ambush in the industrial zone. The force, packing 2 Mandrills, 3 Hermes, and other armor, was shredded by UNCS firepower. A Mandrill, struck by an anti-ST missile, lost its legs and crashed in factory ruins.\nThe Mandrill's pilot, refusing to yield, radioed for backup while battling NDF forces. Using terrain to advantage, they held out for 30 minutes until reinforcements arrived.\nPost-battle, Mandrills shifted to spec-ops roles. Some units were converted to export-grade STs, finding their way to overseas buyers and civilian militias.", "comment": {"by": "Grant", "text": "Anti-ST guns make those behemoths manageable."}}]}, "30090102": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "SEED"}], "introduction": "KX-084 MetalMare\nA heavy assault ST developed by Kamadar.\nEquipped with an SAT-1 gas guidance system made from Arashium alloy, it converts a portion of the engine's power into kinetic energy for the firearm, enhancing the lethality of each shot. With a simple, stable design, it serves as an NDF-certified mobile turret.", "stories": [{"title": "Mobile Gunport", "text": "From inception, the MetalMare ST excels as a mobile artillery platform. Its straightforward design prioritizes firepower and durability over agility. After years of successful deployments, it's becoming the NDF's mainline ST, rolling out across most combat units.", "comment": {"by": "William", "text": "Those blueprints scream elite tech. Give every soldier one of these—ten on the Eastern Front and Thepia would've fallen."}}, {"title": "Firepower Point", "text": "The MetalMare proved crucial in the Battle of White Maple City in XC 111. This intense two-hour clash saw about 70 STs in action, with 45 from the rebel forces. Rebels, using high-speed STs and camo vehicles, smashed through Sunset Valley's outer defenses, rapidly infiltrating the city core. Faced with rebel strike teams swarming the area, the NDF countered with heavy STs. In this showdown, a single MetalMare often suppressed 2-3 standard STs in urban combat, dominating entire city blocks with overwhelming firepower."}, {"title": "Fishnet", "text": "The MetalMares' defense couldn't stop the rebels' kamikaze vehicles from hitting the arms factory and power plant. But the street blockades slowed the assault's spread, shielding most civilian structures. The MetalMares' counterattack halted the rebels' advance. Unable to breach the mech's firepower grid, the rebels failed their tactical goals. Meanwhile, White Maple City's defenders couldn't repel the enemy entirely. They relied on urban cover for a grueling attrition war. The battle concluded when the rebels' supply lines were hit, forcing an early retreat."}, {"title": "Special Operator", "text": "In late 112, Kamadar Military Factory receives a classified lab order to modify MetalMare cockpits—halving size and enhancing pilot sync capabilities. Despite being a small order, Kadrey's military directive fast-tracks production. The compact cockpit proves challenging for standard pilots to operate.", "comment": {"by": "Emily", "text": "Commander, this ST's been my partner. Don't scrap her!"}}]}, "10210102": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "Doll Industries"}], "introduction": "DD-102 Radiance\nThis ST is a prototype mech developed by Doll Industries. It won the Best Appearance Award in an ST Design Competition held by the Dawnstar League.\nThe design of this ST was inspired by sports cars, giving it a sleek and elegant appearance. It offers outstanding performance in reducing resistance and minimizing noise.\nThe Radiance has achieved remarkable results in various counter-terrorism operations. However, due to its high manufacturing cost only a small number of them are currently in service with the regular army.", "stories": [{"title": "Powerful Gale", "text": "Radiance shows strong test metrics in both evasion against heavy fire and multi-point stealth attack accuracy. Uniquely, aerodynamics testing included comparisons with 3 leading sports cars, though no ST benchmarks. Aurora's superior aerodynamics translate to enhanced energy efficiency under standard operations."}, {"title": "Shining Light", "text": "The Radiance mech has been a standout in every counter-terror op. When enemy precision fire pins down other STs, this agile beast breaks through, carving paths for allies. It's the complete package - a killer look with the muscle to back it up. The Radiance proves you can have both style and substance in one lethal machine."}, {"title": "Lightweight Counterattack", "text": "Despite Radiance's design success, initial sales fell short due to high production costs and controversial sports car aesthetics deterring traditional ST buyers. Government subsidies later boosted sales significantly. The Electric Eel Mercenaries now count among Aurora's satisfied users, and military forces deploy limited units as optional combat configurations. Market performance proves Radiance's worth beyond aesthetics. It stands as an innovative work of military engineering.", "comment": {"by": "Naomi", "text": "Electric Eel's nod means something."}}, {"title": "High Score Hymn", "text": "Radiance dominates the 3rd DL ST Design Contest with sports car aesthetics and ultimate mobility. Winner Madeline Jones honors the design team."}]}, "20230102": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "Obsidian"}], "introduction": "OS-10R Roadrunner\nObsidian developed this medium sized ST with a high cost to performance ratio compared to other STs of the same type and generation.\nThis model features a frontal observation device and an external steel frame that can carry additional maintenance equipment. It uses the \"Moho Discontinuity EDGE System\" to improve protection and further reduce costs, which has won it wide acclaim in the market.\nIt is reported that this ST's proprietary technology originally came from the Principality of Ovett.", "stories": [{"title": "Debuted", "text": "Roadrunner achieves superior performance at lower cost through Moho Discontinuity EDGE System. Yegor and Alpha's breakthrough at Royal Research Institute marked advanced armor design evolution."}, {"title": "Small Trouble", "text": "Beyond UKB-1 assignments, Yegor's off-hours are consumed by Steel Trooper R&D. World Bank blockades force him to use cash for parts in the local mech black market. This sketchy behavior attracts unwanted attention. Alpha, his mech, sports colleagues' bootleg components, but it's not enough. Yegor's groundbreaking papers for UNCS and DL journals demand cutting-edge hardware he's yet to acquire.", "comment": {"by": "Naomi", "text": "Roadrunner's weak spot? That rear joint. Maybe not so accidental."}}, {"title": "Crossroads", "text": "Alpha faces dilemma: protect Moho system or pursue personal gain. Chooses to leave Ovett, offering Roadrunner tech to overseas powers for career advancement."}, {"title": "Beyond", "text": "During the Moho Discontinuity EDGE System breach, a Roadrunner mech charged toward a docked cargo ship. Ovett troops engaged, igniting a fierce two-hour battle. The Roadrunner's armor held strong against relentless fire, showcasing the EDGE System's prowess. Design Bureau backup arrived, but the mech escaped with critical damage. Smuggled across the ocean, Obsidian scientists eagerly cracked open the cockpit, only to find the pilot had perished.", "comment": {"by": "Naomi", "text": "The killer blow came from a rival Roadrunner mech. Alpha reached his promised land while Obsidian snagged the coveted tech. A perfect double victory!"}}]}, "30250102": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "UKB-1"}], "introduction": "HU-21 Swampwalker\nThe UKB-1 designed this heavy tactical ST to tackle the unique terrain of jungle regions.\nIt is best suited for providing firepower support during rainforest combat. With its unique joint design and suspension, it can smoothly traverse swamps and maintain balance even under intense fire.", "stories": [{"title": "Jungle Type", "text": "The DLAF commissioned 270 Swampwalkers from UKB-1 to dominate Milkhama's treacherous mangroves. These cutting-edge STs boast revolutionary joint tech and custom suspensions, slicing through swamps and jungles with ease. Dispersed across key outposts, these aquatic assassins stand ready to unleash hell in the wetlands."}, {"title": "The Swamp of Death", "text": "15 Swampwalkers deployed to Siniestro's dense jungles. Mission: Crush the NDF. Guided by satellites, these mech beasts found hidden launch zones. Their cutting-edge joints and suspension conquered the terrain, creating indestructible rocket sites. The DLAF, realizing the Swampwalkers' potential in the steamy rainforest, rushed all units to Siniestro. In one epic clash, they obliterated 5 NDF armored battalions. The invaders? Now just another part of the jungle, tangled in vines and sunk in swamps.", "comment": {"by": "Marcus", "text": "STs seemed invincible, mastering all terrain. Milkhama taught them humility."}}, {"title": "Maintenance Chain", "text": "UNCS special forces, disguised as Siniestro guerrillas, captured two Swampwalkers. DLAF pursuit failed, but built-in self-destruct activated during transport."}, {"title": "Find Another Way", "text": "The genius behind the Swampwalker mech, Azim Amir Khan, secured DL permanent residency and Honorary Citizen status for his groundbreaking work at the ST Institute. Post-DL mission, Khan joined UNCS but tragically ended his life at his Saget Town estate."}]}, "10260101": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "UKB-1"}], "introduction": "HU-04 Aker\nThis light ST was developed by the UKB-1, and is one of the original ST models used in the Milkhama War.\nHighly maneuverable, with thin armor and easy-to-use features, it is mass-produced in all major cities on Milkhama and was once used to escort the Arcus Tactical ST.\nOnce deployed in large numbers with the main force of the NDF, it has since been repurposed for training, surveillance, and patrols, or modified by civilians for security work in peacetime.", "stories": [{"title": "Spear of Assault", "text": "The UKB-1's Aker mecha: frontline warriors and cannon fodder. These mechs swarm Dawnstar defenses, exploiting gaps for deadly encirclements. Packed with user-friendly tech—auto-fire and evasion systems, even rookies can pilot like aces. Aker teams up with Arcus missile launchers for devastating combos. Mass-produced in every major city to feed the war machine."}, {"title": "Operation Breakthrough", "text": "Despite losses to DL artillery, Aker units showcase 60% breakthrough rate, clearing trenches and fire points with superior mobility."}, {"title": "Ashes of War", "text": "Veterans of the NDF recall the ST Aker as their steadfast companion through countless battles. Post-war, it transitioned to support roles in secondary units, handling training, recon, and patrol duties."}, {"title": "Reuse", "text": "Retired Akers found new purpose in civilian life as production units and security assets. Some treat them as mechanical pets. In private hangars, you might spot custom-painted Akers, readied for shows or personal display."}]}, "30020101": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "Laniakea"}], "introduction": "LTX-32 Centurion\nA Heavy ST produced by Laniakea. One of the original ST models used in the Milkhama War.\nThe design of the Centurion was based on the popular turretless tank design at the time, with polycrystalline ceramic coating on the surface and movable armor protecting the head. This design significantly reduced manufacturing difficulty and increased pilot survival rates. In tactical situations, it often cooperated with the Tiktaalik. It became the mainstay model of the NDF.", "stories": [{"title": "Special Design", "text": "ST Centurion saw mass deployment in XC 99. Its fixed-head design with armored sensors draws from turretless tanks, boosting pilot survival in heavy fire while simplifying production.", "comment": {"by": "Grant", "text": "I could run the elevated track blindfolded in this ST. Cannon fodder units don't need flash, just reliability and tight handling."}}, {"title": "Tactical Application", "text": "ST Centurion typically draws fire while ST Tiktaalik strikes from flanks. At Golden Nuggets, Centurions support ST Gillesrais in positional counterattacks."}, {"title": "Battle of the Golden Nuggets", "text": "In August, DLAF secured northern highlands at Golden Nuggets, repelling NDF attacks. Their artillery suppresses town defenses while surveillance exposes garrison positions. A covert ST Centurion operation emerges as the response."}, {"title": "Victory Type", "text": "The NDF strikes back with 55 ST Centurions and two ST Gillesrais from south and west. Their armor endures enemy fire as troops sever DLAF's eastern support. After losing half their forces, DLAF retreats to Lorine Mountains.", "comment": {"by": "Grant", "text": "Poly-ceramic coating? That's civilian tech. Hard to fix and can't match modern composite armor's punch."}}]}, "20350101": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "Obsidian"}], "introduction": "OS-04 Cyclone\nA Medium ST, developed by Obsidian. This ST played a crucial role as a firepower support platform for the DL during the Milkhama War.\nThis ST is powered by the MA-3000 engine, which was independently developed by Obsidian and is equipped with prefabricated frames, enabling compatibility with multiple heavy weapons.\nAfter the war, the Cyclone was phased out of by front line forces, but remains a powerful asset in the Ashes arsenal.", "stories": [{"title": "Type: Support", "text": "In the Milkhama War's early phase, NDF strike teams targeted isolated DL flanks, aiming to sever comms and obliterate them. The DLAF realized they needed agile support STs to match their mobile units' pace. Conventional artillery lagged behind the swift ST squadrons. Seizing this combat niche, Obsidian's Cyclone STs scored big with Dawnstar League contracts."}, {"title": "Simple Structure", "text": "The Cyclone: Obsidian's early-gen fire support mech. Packing the custom MA-3000 engine, this bad boy's got folding alloy frames throughout its chassis. Whether you're hefting heavy artillery or launching missiles, these frames keep your weapons steady. Load it up with SEED's 240 boom-sticks or Horizon's 310 inferno rockets. This mech takes 'em all!"}, {"title": "Circulation", "text": "During the war's initial phase, the Cyclone ST was the DL's ace in the hole for close-range firepower. These mecha beasts held the line against overwhelming UNCS forces, defying the odds time and again. Post-war, the DL opted to streamline their ST arsenal, but they had a trick up their sleeve. Instead of scrapping the retired Cyclones, they covertly offloaded them to West Milkhama's rebels. The kicker? A good chunk of these badass STs ended up with the Ashes, ready to give the NDF one hell of a surprise.", "comment": {"by": "Marcus", "text": "Found a used Cyclone—UNCS trophy, dead security pilot, salvage market special."}}, {"title": "Profit Winner", "text": "The Ashes modified captured Cyclone STs to fight UNCS forces, protecting bases and seizing equipment in mountain and desert warfare. The Dawnstar League profited beyond mere scrap fees.", "comment": {"by": "Marcus", "text": "DLAF deal was pure business."}}]}, "20360101": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "UKB-1"}], "introduction": "HU-06 Ergate\nA Medium ST, improved and upgraded by the UKB-1 based on the civil SL - KS-1.\nExported by the Ovett Principality and deployed worldwide, this ST has some of the strongest armor and module interchangeability among first generation STs and performs well in large-scale group combat on the front line.\nAlthough its performance is inferior to primary battle STs, it is reliable, inexpensive, and easy-to-maintain. These characteristics make it standard for second-line troops and various civilian armed groups.", "stories": [{"title": "Common Styles", "text": "The Ergate: a workhorse mech for second-line troops and civilian militias. Even third-rate groups like the Eburgo Militia and Siniestro Lumberjacks snag and mod these discarded machines for farm defense. But dig deeper, and you'll find the Ergate's got a combat-rich past in the far-off Principality of Ovett. This ST unit's no slouch in its early days!"}, {"title": "KS-1", "text": "Ergate started as KS-1, farm bot for western plains. Heavy lifter, reliable worker. When armor units got chewed up in the Brush Fire War, enemy rolled through grain country. Ovett's answer? Slap armor on farm bots at the tractor plant, arm them, rush them to the front."}, {"title": "Ant Colony", "text": "Over 3500 KS-1 STs join the battle with 1800 destroyed. The survivors and Thunderous ST Squad push forward like steel tide, turning the tide. Post-war, UKB-1 upgrades make KS-1s nearly indestructible in groups."}, {"title": "Steel Exiles", "text": "KS-1's success stems from Ovett's vast industrial workforce becoming skilled pilots, unmatched by DL or UNCS. As Ovett transforms to a Principality, pilot shortages lead to mass ST sales. The free world dubs it: Ergate.", "comment": {"by": "Grant", "text": "Scored mine at a junkyard, limbs in pieces but engine and targeting intact. Fixed her up good. Check that manipulator arm, sweet tech, right?"}}]}, "20370101": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "Laniakea"}], "introduction": "LTX-27 Falcon\nA Medium ST developed by Laniakea and specializing in achieving accurate and economical ranged attacks.\nThe Falcon is equipped with the \"Sparrow\" optical sight, lending it excellent firing accuracy. The strength of its other parts is equivalent to the civilian model. This model performs outstandingly in low-intensity regular combat but is put to the test in complex three-dimensional battlefields.", "stories": [{"title": "Cost Control", "text": "Falcon, at 130,000 Milkhama Dollars, delivers combat efficiency. Laniakea excels in basic models too. While all-round performance at low cost proves challenging, focused reinforcement succeeds for stationary combat roles."}, {"title": "Cheap and Useful", "text": "The Falcon's final price tag: 123,000 Milkhama Dollars. A steal among sharpshooter STs! Laniakea's 65k MHD \"Sparrow\" optics boost its mid-range firepower in harsh conditions. Other parts? Civilian-grade tough. In standard combat, these sniper STs find their sweet spot. That's when Falcon's precision strike capability truly soars!"}, {"title": "General Audience", "text": "Border warfare evolves to 3D combat. \"Deep assault + infiltration strikes\" tactics challenge low-mobility STs dependent on sniper positions. Recent years see military Falcons transitioning to civilian use."}, {"title": "Promising Future", "text": "Laniakea explores Falcon's border war potential through drone support integration, enhanced info-warfare, and new composite armor. These upgrades maintain precision strike capability. Future models remain uncertain amid escalating tensions."}]}, "10080101": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "An-Holt"}], "introduction": "AST-03 Lanius\nThis light ST was developed by An-Holt, and is one of the original ST models used in the Milkhama War.\nIt is equipped with B-type anti-impact cushions inside the legs and knees, and the head is fitted with a reinforced signal transceiver that allows for rapid troop assembly after landing.\nInitially designed for airborne units to operate with Meister, most surviving Lanius units are utilized by second-line forces.", "stories": [{"title": "Soaring Bird", "text": "The Lanius: an airborne mech with B-type shock absorbers in its knees. This agile fighter was key to smashing UNCS lines. Its specialized comms array lets it sync seamlessly with the DLAF's heavy hitter, Meister, for flawless squad ops."}, {"title": "Airborne Assault", "text": "Before the last major conflict, the DL foresaw ground assault challenges and engineered elite STs for airborne ops. 7 hours into the Southern Frontier Clash, 70 Lanius mecha dropped 150 clicks behind enemy lines. These metal warriors obliterated 2 NDF ammo caches and 5 anti-tank nests before blazing west. Their surgical strike enabled frontline forces to lock down the Southern Border in a vise-like pincer move.", "comment": {"by": "Grant", "text": "How to find your squad after drop? Try encrypted comms first. If there is no response in 10 mins, resort to bird calls in zone chat."}}, {"title": "Tactical Changes", "text": "Lanius made its name striking deep behind UNCS lines. Now with advanced ground-air defenses, airborne STs are losing their edge. Biggest hurdle: organizing fast after drops while staying off radar long enough to survive."}, {"title": "Reliable Part", "text": "The ST Lanius serves in auxiliary forces, handling low-intensity combat, security ops, and training recruits. Battle-tested reliability makes it a trustworthy machine. Its signature shock-absorbing legs are now popular in civilian engineering, proving especially effective in jungle and hilly terrain."}]}, "30130101": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "Obsidian"}], "introduction": "OS-02 Meister\nThis Heavy ST was produced by Obsidian, and is one of the original ST models used in the Milkhama War.\nAll parts are designed with detachable interfaces for easy assembly and disassembly. Sufficient armor plates can be added, and damaged parts can be easily repaired. During deployment, it often worked in conjunction with the Lanius. Since the war, parts from retired units can be easily found on the black market.", "stories": [{"title": "Meister Ready", "text": "Armored Battalion 304 to Captain Steve. Lieutenant Wright requesting support. Our advance is halted by NDFs fortified west river crossing. Wounded evacuated and fresh pilots ready. Need 10+ heavy STs, preferably Meisters, to breach their defenses.", "comment": {"by": "Naomi", "text": "Found Lt. Wright's old request: 10 Meisters needed. Those things were everywhere in the Milkhama War."}}, {"title": "About Belief", "text": "\"Heard the army's got new STs. Our old Scouts won't stand a chance in the next defense...\"\n\"No defeatist talk! Battle's about spirit, not gear!\"\n\"But we don't even have Shrikes for combat support...\"\n\"That your excuse? Get in those cockpits, now!\"", "comment": {"by": "Diracca", "text": "Meister STs deploy with Lanius for mobility support and flank protection."}}, {"title": "Know the Drill", "text": "Captain Steve, our Meister squad has been depleted. You've received the wreckage returns, and factoring in recycling value, I'm requesting 15 more units. These STs are invaluable at the frontline, even farm hands master them easily. If salvage logistics prove burdensome, I could arrange local disposal and convert to Milkhama currency. The local scrappers are always eager for ST components.—Lieutenant Wright"}, {"title": "Who?", "text": "\"Fire support needed at Hill 701!\"\n\"Fire now—traitors in Meisters took our position!\"\n\"Damn rebels coming in hot—can't stop these Meisters!\"\n\"304th Armor, fall back east—we're overrun!\"", "comment": {"by": "Naomi", "text": "Run, Lt. Wright, run! Border militia's packing heat thanks to you!"}}]}, "20310101": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "Laniakea"}], "introduction": "LTX-22 Tiktaalik\nA Medium ST developed by Laniakea and extensively deployed by the NDF during the Milkhama War.\nThis ST utilizes advanced armor processing technology and is equipped with basic optical observation systems on the head and chest sides, providing specific frontal combat capabilities.\nDue to its simple and reliable characteristics it is still active in various areas of the UNCS.", "stories": [{"title": "Warfire Reincarnation", "text": "Tiktaalik, cost-effective and modular like many post-war STs, maintains combat effectiveness with interchangeable parts. Against Dawnstar League's Aker and Cyclone forces, UNCS pilots deploy Tiktaalik forming a dependable attrition front."}, {"title": "Steel Wolf Pack", "text": "Tiktaalik-Centurion teams excel in combat. Centurion suppresses enemy defenses while Tiktaalik infiltrates positions. Despite intensified frontline combat, NDF favors this cost-effective combo due to mutual restraint."}, {"title": "Production Standards", "text": "Quality tests confirm new Tiktaalik units meet production standards in materials and craftsmanship. Built to latest UNCS ST manual by Laniakea, Dorn Metal, Freeman Industries, and Northern Hemisphere Mining. Clark Bluecher's standards revision, following proposals and audits under Gordon Bluecher's supervision, adjusts Tiktaalik specifications.", "comment": {"by": "Yevgeny", "text": "He's struggling each step. Sustainability's questionable. Let the Ashes handle this."}}, {"title": "Some Upgrades", "text": "Fresh Tiktaalik had issues against rebels. Engineers fixed that—universal parts for quick frontline repairs. Now it stays in the fight longer, especially alongside Centurions.", "comment": {"by": "Yevgeny", "text": "Skip the patches, build new."}}]}, "10250101": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "Laniakea"}], "introduction": "NED-00 Ursprung\nA prototype ST designed and produced by Laniakea. \nOriginally designed to carry a specialization unit called the \"Testee,\" this ST was eventually dismantled for unknown reasons.\nOnly a few of these models exist. Their overall performance is slightly higher than the first-generation models currently deployed.", "stories": [{"title": "Unknown ST", "text": "Laniakea's Origin Lab created Ursprung as a verification model. Advanced frame optimizes close combat, originally equipped with \"Testee\" unit. Modifications reduced performance to slightly above standard STs.", "comment": {"by": "Naomi", "text": "Just a nickname, no official designation."}}, {"title": "Hidden Potential", "text": "Lab tests reveal control complexity issues. Designer Bolser views Ursprung as unfinished but promising, suggesting advanced successor models. Designer Harrison maintains silence on assessment.", "comment": {"by": "Naomi", "text": "Kaidan started with Ursprung. Claims it was for practice, really needed cash."}}, {"title": "Moment of Decision", "text": "Ursprung's production faced complications due to GSA intel revealing tech theft risks. Designer Harrison removed core \"Testee\" unit, hiding it in a friend's warehouse before delivering low-performance units to military."}, {"title": "Easy Experiment", "text": "The performance and reception of the Ursprung, despite its high potential, have been disappointing, with elite pilots rejecting it and recruits struggling with its complexity.\nHarrison knows that this is not the end of Ursprung. The unutilized \"Testee\" unit, harboring Laniakea's cutting-edge technology, indicates a promising future for follow-up models."}]}, "30310101": {"profile": [{"label": "Manufacturer", "value": "Horizon"}], "introduction": "HR-605 Zealred\nA Heavy ST developed by Horizon, it was one of the original ST models used in the Milkhama War.\nIt achieves high armor and modularity with low production costs and ample production capacity. Its armed mount system adopts a modular component design compatible with various assault weapons.", "stories": [{"title": "New Era, Old Era", "text": "The tides finally turned. Orders streamed into the machine factories once more. Grinders brought rusty machines back to life, sparks dancing between chrome steel and spinning wheels. Molds emerged from old newspaper wrappings, cleaned and mounted on massive presses. Workers returned - some to barracks, others to assembly lines. Their sweat and toil, mixed with mechanical thunder, awakened the Dawnstar League's dormant economy. Every component promised a brighter tomorrow. Zealred stepped out to cheers: a new era of tech and Steel Troopers had begun.", "comment": {"by": "Worker (Male)", "text": "Pre-Milkhama days were sweet. Factory humming, evening beers, sausages with crew."}}, {"title": "Survival", "text": "Zealred STs board trains for Foren River like giants on steel snakes, facing survival or death among the gunfire."}, {"title": "Idle Type", "text": "Post-war Zealreds serve new purpose - combat dummies for Gillesrais testing. Set to autonomous mode, these abandoned STs measure strike force capabilities."}, {"title": "Destination", "text": "When memories fade of this mechanical age, they'll recall Rustville's sprawling scrapyards. Battered Zealreds arrive on heavy haulers, their frontline service ended. Thick armor cracked and punctured, a tangle of exposed wiring caked in mud and oil awaits its fate. This is the Zealred graveyard - final rest for battle-worn STs. Some still serve, while others feed the furnace, reborn in steel, their battles forgotten.", "comment": {"by": "Arnold", "text": "Post-ceasefire, Rustville boomed. Jobs soared, economy bounced back—textbook recovery."}}]}};
